\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Stronger Early As Market Mulls Signs From Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2010\par 13:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real strengthened in early trading Thursday as investors looked expectantly for signs of recovery in Europe and a resolution to that region's recent fiscal woes.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.702 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.706 to the dollar in the previous session Wednesday on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the real gained ground after the euro zone posted third-quarter economic growth within market expectations. The region reported 1.9% growth versus the same quarter in 2009 and 0.4% growth from the second quarter this year.\par \par \uc2 Investors, meanwhile, will be looking to remarks Thursday by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet to gauge whether the region will continue to recover from the fiscal difficulties of some member countries, such as Ireland, Spain, Greece and Portugal.\par \par \uc2 Locally, attention remains fixed on possible government actions to limit strengthening of the real.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government in October raised taxes on incoming investment to discourage inflows from short-term investment. While the move had a short-term effect in slowing inflows, recent data have shown dollar flows resuming due to abundant global liquidity.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is expected to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday with customary dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The bank in recent months had stepped up its dollar purchase auctions to two daily as part of an effort to contain the strengthening of the real and build the country's foreign reserves. In recent days, however, it has limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to one auction per session.\par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves stood at $285.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 02-12-10 1217GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101202e6c2000ys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
