\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Strengthens Early Tracking Local Data, Euro\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2010\par 14:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real strengthened in early trading Thursday amid encouragement from upbeat local economic data and a slight firming of the euro.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.7195 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.722 to the dollar Wednesday on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the market was seeing low trading volume Thursday as a reflection of closed U.S. markets for the Thanksgiving holiday.\par \par \uc2 After early declines, the euro showed a slight rebound as investors considered improved prospects for the recovery of Euro zone economies from recent fiscal crises.\par \par \uc2 The trend provided a boost for metals and other key commodities exported by Brazil.\par \par \uc2 At the same time Thursday, investors took encouragement from a continued trend of improving local economic data.\par \par \uc2 The latest favorable signals were brought by Brazilian unemployment, which fell 6.1% in October from 6.2% in September according to Brazil's IBGE statistics institute. The rate came in line with market expectations and was the best on record for a second month running.\par \par \uc2 Investors Thursday were also celebrating an apparent change of heart by local economic authorities regarding government fiscal policies.\par \par \uc2 In accepting to stay on during the incoming administration of Brazil's president-elect Dilma Rousseff, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said the government planned to curtail spending in 2011 in an effort to help cut local interest rates and debt.\par \par \uc2 Markets reacted to the announcement by showing a noticeable decline in yields on local debt.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is expected to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday with customary dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The bank in recent months has stepped up its dollar purchase auctions to two daily as part of an effort to contain the strengthening of the real and build the country's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, Brazil's reserves stood at $285.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 25-11-10 1323GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101125e6bp00101\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
