\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Early As Market Looks To G-20 Meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2010\par 12:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened in early trading Monday as investors mulled the possibility of moves to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at a meeting of G-20 member nations this week.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.6930 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.6793 to the dollar Friday on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost ground early Monday after posting some gains late last week.\par \par \uc2 The latest trend comes as investors look ahead to the possible outcomes of a meeting of G-20 member nation leaders in South Korea this week to discuss a resolution for recent rounds of competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations among countries which have been dubbed "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars."\par \par \uc2 While analysts have expressed little hope for concrete measures at the meeting, expectations have grown that world leaders could signal possible policy directions ahead.\par \par \uc2 The weakening of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, comes amid signals for a contrary movement locally.\par \par \uc2 Among those include rising inflation forecasts and continued expectations of rising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 According to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released Monday, economists revised year-end projections for Brazil's IPCA consumer price index this year upward to an average 5.31% from 5.29% seen the previous week. The projection remains well above the government's year-end inflation target of 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's reference Selic interest rate, meanwhile, is seen rising to 11.75% by the end of 2011 from 10.75% currently.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is expected to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets Monday with a customary dollar purchases on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The bank in recent months has stepped up its dollar purchase auctions to two daily as part of an effort to contain the strengthening of the real and build the country's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 As of Friday, Brazil's reserves stood at $287.2 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 08-11-10 1158GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101108e6b8001b1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
