\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real firms ahead of Fed, pesos mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2010\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on U.S. Federal Reserve statement at 1815 GMT\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real jumps 0.7 pct, Mexican peso gains 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso weakens 0.3 on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears (Adds context about \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged on Wednesday while Mexico's peso hit a 6-month high ahead of a likely announcement on monetary stimulus measures in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve is widely expected to announce after 2:15 p.m. EDT (1815 GMT) asset purchases of at least $500 billion via quantitative easing -- in effect printing money to buy bonds and lower borrowing costs. For more, see: [ID:nLDE6A2062]\par \par \uc2 That should keep yields on U.S. Treasuries close to record lows, encouraging investors to buy Latin America's higher-yielding bonds.\par \par \uc2 Brazil is a prime target because the country's benchmark interest rate of 10.75 percent is one of the highest in the world.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> surged as much as 1.1 percent in early trading on Wednesday and was later up 0.70 percent at 1.694 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 The real was also pricing in the region's gains on Tuesday, when Brazil's markets were closed for a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 "The market was shut yesterday, so there was a movement in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the real wasn't able to follow. But to a great extent, (the real is stronger) in anticipation of the results of the Fed meeting," said Marianna Costa, an economist with Link Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "Anything close to $500 billion is already priced into the market. If it was something closer to $1 trillion, there could be some more space for appreciation. If it is less (than $500 billion), the market, like everywhere else in the world, is not going to take it well."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> edged up to its strongest level since May 3, later trading 0.10 percent stronger at 12.2927 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the Fed will move to purchase the expected $500 billion in bonds and the peso won't see a huge move after the announcement," said Alfredo Puig, a trader at Vector brokerage in Monterrey, Mexico.\par \par \uc2 But if the amount is less than expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rapidly weaken to 12.38, he added.\par \par \uc2 Some economists say the peso could outperform the region's other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the months ahead because of the country's hands-off approach to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. [ID:nN0147422]\par \par \uc2 WAITING TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 Other governments across the region have taken a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, such as dollar purchases and capital controls, to slow rallies in their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes exports more expensive abroad and can cause long-term damage to a country's economy.\par \par \uc2 For example, data this week is expected to show that Brazil's industrial output slowed again last month because of the strong real.\par \par \uc2 Fears of new measures hit the Chilean peso <CLP=> on Wednesday. It weakened 0.33 percent to 488.6 per dollar. [ID:nN30113748]\par \par \uc2 "There are rumors in the market that after the Fed's decision, some new measures will be taken here to curb the peso," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The peso has strengthened 12 percent since the end of June as the country has recovered rapidly from a devastating earthquake in February.\par \par \uc2 President Sebastian Pinera said last week his government is working to open capital accounts and relax limits on investments abroad to battle the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also go back to buying dollars in the market or find others ways to encourage capital outflows. [ID:nN20242719] (Additional reporting by Caroline Stauffer and Noe Torres in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101106e6b30009l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
