\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2-Brazil sees benign prices; Meirelles warns on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2010\par 16:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Policy-makers see benign inflation scenario\par \par \uc2 * Meirelles warns on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures to protect economy\par \par \uc2 * Despite pressures, inflation seen converging to target\par \par \uc2 * Yields on rate futures firm after minutes (Adds Mantega comment on creation of IMF index in 8th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By Elzio Barreto\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled Thursday that it is unlikely to raise interest rates in coming months, though concerns over food prices and an overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to hover over an otherwise robust economy.\par \par \uc2 In minutes from last week's monetary policy meeting, at which the bank left rates unchanged, policymakers said they saw inflation falling closer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 4.5 percent, plus or minus 2 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 The outlook underscored the bank's belief that Brazil's economy remains in a charmed pattern of high growth and relatively low inflation, despite some pressure from rising food prices and robust consumer demand.\par \par \uc2 "The assumption is that this (recent) hump in inflation will be temporary, despite the heated economy," said Zeina Latif, senior Latin America economist at RBS in Sao Paulo. "There are risks, of course, but I see no problem in keeping rates stable and waiting for more signs."\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on the Selic rate: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/pup68k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/pup68k}}}\par \par \uc2 Graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p}}}\par \par \uc2 Analysis on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform: [ID:nN26120199]\par \par \uc2 Factbox on political risks in Brazil: [ID:nRISKBR]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Instead, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles focused on what seems to be the biggest risk to Brazil's economy at the moment -- the real, which like the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of many other emerging markets is strengthening against a weak U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Meirelles urged that the world's largest economies agree on coordinated efforts to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility at next month's meeting of G20 leaders in South Korea. However, he suggested Brazil could go its own way until a deal is reached.\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, while we don't get there, each country will have to take measures to protect their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Meirelles told reporters in Sao Paulo. "We are taking action to protect the Brazilian economy."\par \par \uc2 In an interview with daily O Globo on Thursday, Finance Minister Guido Mantega echoed the call for action, suggesting the International Monetary Fund should create an index to measure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation by different countries. [ID:nN28110123]\par \par \uc2 NO RATE MOVE\par \par \uc2 This year Brazil's economy, the largest in Latin America, is set to grow more than 7 percent -- its fastest pace in more than two decades, boosted by public works projects and a surge in credit.\par \par \uc2 The rapid expansion pressured consumer prices as more and more Brazilians line up to buy new cars, homes and appliances, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise borrowing costs by 2 percentage points between April and September before pausing.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Selic rate, at 10.75 percent, is among the highest in the world and is attracting a flood of U.S. dollars from overseas investors that has sparked a 5 percent rally in the Brazilian real <BRBY><BRL=> since the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Recent data point to an improved balance of risks for government administered prices, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic policy committee, known as Copom, said in the minutes. Still, the bank said is ready to change monetary policy quickly if pressures on consumer prices increase.\par \par \uc2 Analysts in a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey expect the Selic to stay at 10.75 percent through the end of 2010, leaving it for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials in Brazil's next administration to decide whether to hike rates to keep prices in check.\par \par \uc2 All polls released recently forecast Brazilian ruling party candidate Dilma Rousseff winning a runoff vote on Sunday by a wide margin. One of her biggest challenges will be to control government spending in a bid to slow the economy and ease pressures on inflation.\par \par \uc2 "In the minutes, they're basically saying they will not move, period. But unless there is a real fiscal consolidation, I mean real consolidation, by the second quarter of 2011 reality will sink in," said Pedro Tuesta, senior Latin America economist at research firm 4Cast Inc in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures contracts <0#DIJ:> were little changed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes. The yield on the contract due January 2012 <DIJF2> dipped to 11.35 percent from 11.36 percent on late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Food prices that have surged in recent weeks are pressuring inflation more than in the recent past, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken those risks into consideration, the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 "Despite that, at this moment it remains our understanding that the convergence of inflation to the center of the target will likely happen," policymakers said in the minutes. (Additional reporting by Mariane Pinho, Guillermo Parra-Bernal and Todd Benson; Editing by Brian Winter, Chizu Nomiyama and Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101028e6as001yy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
