\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil ready to use swaps to curb real - report\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2010\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * No legal obstacles to measure, ready to be used\par \par \uc2 * Reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps last used regularly in Sept. 2008\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to use reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps in an effort to curb a recent rally in the real, the Valor Economico newspaper reported in its online edition.\par \par \uc2 "Reverse swaps is a mechanism that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can use at any moment," said Aldo Mendes, the bank's director of monetary policy, according to Valor. "The legal conditions for its use are in place," he added.\par \par \uc2 Reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps are a form of derivative, which would effectively allow Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 Investors have mulled use of the swaps since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested the market's demand on July 23, but they have gone off radar screens as the focus turned to other measures.\par \par \uc2 Brazil recently stepped up its dollar purchases in the spot market in an effort to slow a recent rally in the real <BRBY>, which is hurting exporters and worsening the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The government also this month tripled its tax on foreign bond purchases to 6 percent and raised a tax on the collateral investors must put down to trade in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p}}}\par \par \uc2 Analysis on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform: [ID:nN26120199]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Under the reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap agreement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agrees to pay investors Brazil's local interbank rate in exchange for a rate in U.S. dollars for the duration of the contract.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began offering reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps in February 2005, used them regularly until September 2008, and then once more on May 5, 2009. (Reporting by Samantha Pearson; Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /SWAPS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101027e6ar00196\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
