\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil's Meirelles: Too soon for new inflows actions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2010\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds comment, market prices)\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Oct 26 (Reuters) - Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Henrique Meirelles said on Tuesday that all the necessary actions are being taken to prevent a bubble from occurring due to capital flows into the country.\par \par \uc2  Meirelles, asked about possible new measures to slow inflows that have caused Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen, said authorities needed to see the effect of measures already taken.\par \par \uc2  "The market is volatile, precisely because of these measures. The market is reacting to news based on anonymous sources. So we have to wait for a while to see the effect of these measures to wait for the market to stabilize," Meirelles said on the sidelines of the Buttonwood Gathering, sponsored by The Economist magazine.\par \par \uc2  Brazil adopted a policy of sterilizing investment inflows into the economy  -- issuing local notes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to pay investors from whom it buys dollars -- to try to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, from appreciating too far or too fast while also adopting rules to stop investors from taking excessive risk in the credit markets.\par \par \uc2  "The most dangerous part of the equation is when you have a bubble which is basically generated by credit expansion," Meirelles said.\par \par \uc2  While Brazil's financial system has "solid conditions," inflows -- the result of a healthy pace of economic growth and "high level of liquidity in the U.S. and some other economies" -- are creating a challenging environment because of the surge of portfolio and fixed investments, he said.\par \par \uc2  "The question again is to keep the equilibrium, to keep the balance in the economy, not to allow for that excess liquidity to create the kind of imbalances which are showing now to be so negative and creating so many losses for so many countries," Meirelles said.\par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the real traded down 0.47 percent at 1.7070 per U.S. dollar <BRBY>. The yield on the 10 percent, real-denominated bond due in January 2013, the most widely traded among the so-called NTN-F notes <BR3YT=RR>, fell for the first day in six, shedding 5 basis points to 11.96 percent. The yield was 12.01 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2  In the past month, Brazil has tripled a tax on foreign investment in local bonds and tightened potential loopholes to make the tax more effective.\par \par \uc2  Those measures, along with fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have had some impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real is still up about 6 percent against the U.S. dollar since late June.\par \par \uc2  Speculation has mounted that the government is planning fresh measures to curb inflows to fixed-income markets. However, Brasilia on Monday ruled out new capital gains taxes on foreign holdings of local bonds to curb the real's rally.\par \par \uc2  "At the end of the day, I would call the overall measures taken in general as prudential rules," Meirelles added.  (Additional reporting by William Schomberg in New York and Daniela Machado and Guillermo Parra Bernal in Sao Paulo; Editing by Leslie Adler)   \par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-MEIRELLES/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|MNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101026e6aq001el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
