\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  battle endangers  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reform\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2010\par 17:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Convertibility would attract even more \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation\par \par \uc2 * Global "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" to leave permanent scars\par \par \uc2 * Offshore NDF trading boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's battle to slow a recent rally in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is jeopardizing plans to open the real to international trading.\par \par \uc2 With a view to one day becoming a major financial hub with as much clout as Hong Kong or New York, Brazil has been working to transform the real into a so-called convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That means putting behind it a past of painful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crises and lifting heavy restrictions on the real <BRBY>.\par \par \uc2 But in recent months the government has taken a step backward, introducing even more regulation to the market in an effort to curb a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally that is hurting exporters and undermining the competitiveness of the Brazilian economy.\par \par \uc2 "It makes policymakers more reluctant to pursue full convertibility under these circumstances," said Mike Moran, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in New York.\par \par \uc2 "They will continue to say this is their long term goal, but in the immediate future, the prospect for full convertibility for the likes of Brazil is very weak."\par \par \uc2 Currently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  permits only a few big banks to trade in the local market, making \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions more costly and time-consuming for everybody else.\par \par \uc2 But if these restrictions were lifted, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems would be even worse, some analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have flocked to Brazil partly due to its high-yielding bonds. The deluge of cash has boosted the real, making it one of the world's most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Convertibility? Forget about it," says Carlos Gandolfo, a partner at Sao Paulo's Pioneer brokerage. A freely tradable real would attract even more hot money, or "motel money" as it is known locally -- thrill-seeking investors who are in and out of the country in hours.\par \par \uc2 That is exactly the type of investor \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been fending off with recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, such as tax rises on foreign purchases of bonds. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p }}}\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Convertibility could also bring more volatility to the market, as has been the case in Mexico, one of the few countries in Latin America to have a convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BATTLE SCARS\par \par \uc2 In March this year, Brazil's trading institutions got together to launch 'Brain' -- the latest project to transform the country into a financial superpower, with one of its goals being to free up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The project has been on hold for the past three to four months because of Brazil's ongoing presidential election, said Alan Gandelman, chief executive officer of the Brazil division of ICAP, the world's biggest interdealer broker.\par \par \uc2 "The government wouldn't want (convertibility) now with the real at these levels, but maybe four or five years down the road it could be achieved," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, it could take even longer if the global battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dominated a G20 meeting last week, proves to be part of a long-term structural shift.\par \par \uc2 "There has been a mistrust of what you used to call the Washington Consensus of freely open capital markets, freely convertible, freely floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Win Thin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 But convertibility is not just up to the government: the market also has to want it.\par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were done "in a way to lead investors to believe that the risk of that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen because of the force of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think it could have an effect," said Gustavo Loyola, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, Chile has taken softer measures to deal with its rallying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , partly for fear that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will delay plans to make the peso convertible.\par \par \uc2 Despite its small size, Chile also dreams of becoming Latin America's financial hub.\par \par \uc2 Judging by the non-deliverable forward market, investors are souring on trading the real.\par \par \uc2 NDFs are derivatives that simulate trading in restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the real. The contracts are mostly traded in New York and settled in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Trading in Brazilian NDFs is facing long-term decline and should eventually die out when the real becomes convertible, as has happened in other developing countries such as Russia.\par \par \uc2 But after the government's tax rise last week on futures contracts, ICAP saw volumes in Brazilian NDFs soar about 20-30 percent, said Anna Didier, head of NDFs for the broker.\par \par \uc2 Other investors are weighing costs and contemplating coming back to the market, she said, because even though NDFs are expensive, the rules of the game are more transparent.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone is going back to the drawing board." (Additional reporting by Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo, Ana Nicolaci da Costa in Brasilia, and Caroline Stauffer in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /REFORM (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|ABX|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101029e6aq0026f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
