\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-INTERVIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  sees no limit to  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 19:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Govt will do what is needed to contain real - Augustin\par \par \uc2 * Treasury seeking to expand real debt market abroad\par \par \uc2 * To do 2-3 more issuances of real debt this year (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 By Ana Nicolaci da Costa and Isabel Versiani\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Brazil will spare no efforts to arrest excessive gains in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is looking at expanding its real-denominated debt market abroad, Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin said in an interview on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government has increased efforts to contain a rally in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Last Wednesday it sold real-denominated debt in global markets for the first time since June 2007 in an effort to reduce capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have been flocking to Latin America's largest economy as Brazil's 10.75 percent lending rate offers an attractive alternative to ultra-low interest rates in advanced economies. Those inflows helped take Brazil's real <BRBY> to two-year highs earlier this month. For more, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p}}}\uc2 ].\par \par \uc2 "The government is placing no limits on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we will do whatever is necessary," Augustin told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 In the past month, Brazil's government has tripled a tax on foreign investment in local bonds and tightened potential loopholes to make the tax more effective. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also continued to buy dollars in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Those measures, along with fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have had some impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real is still up about 6 percent since late June.\par \par \uc2 For the Treasury, one option is to build a stronger real-denominated debt market abroad to arrest the flows of capital into Brazil.\par \par \uc2 "This means having a bigger volume, much bigger than we have today," Augustin said.\par \par \uc2 The government plans to issue global bonds denominated in reais at least another two or three times this year, he said. Brazil last week sold $597 million of real-denominated bonds due 2028, but Augustin said the next issuance would likely be in a shorter, 10-year maturity.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has the conditions to launch a 100-year bond, Augustin added, after Mexico launched Latin America's first century bond earlier this month. [ID:nN05194972].\par \par \uc2 "It's a possibility," he said. "Brazil today has very solid fundamentals and this allows us to have debt in the maturity we deem adequate."\par \par \uc2 Augustin did not rule out further increases in a tax on foreign investment in local bonds or the possibility of once again extending the settlement period for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts, as authorities did earlier in October, to allow the Treasury to buy more dollars in the local market. [ID:nN06284208].\par \par \uc2 For the most recent measures, please see: [ID:nN18280200] and [ID:nN14246085] for possible future measures. (Editing by Elzio Barreto, Diane Craft and Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 2, PIX)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101028e6ap0025i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
