\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latin American  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm after G20\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 14:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Traders resume dollar selling after G20 meeting\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.5 pct, Mexican peso gains 0.3 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso hits highest level since early May\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso adds 0.5 pct as copper price soars\par \par \uc2 (Adds data on Brazil's current account, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed early on Monday as the dollar suffered broad losses following an agreement over the weekend from a Group of 20 nations meeting in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers of the G20 group of rich and emerging nations vowed to shun competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations, agreeing that exchange rates should be determined by the market.\par \par \uc2 Investors took this as a green light to resume the status quo in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, which has been to sell the dollar on expectations the Federal Reserve will soon unveil a second round of quantitative easing. [ID:nTOE69M004]\par \par \uc2 "As is often the case with such meetings, the communique that followed the G20 meeting has been deemed to be vague," said Jane Foley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have enjoyed a multi-week rally because of speculation over U.S. stimulus measures, which are likely to keep yields on U.S. Treasuries close to record lows and so encourage more investors to buy higher-yielding debt in countries such as \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But fears of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have helped to keep a lid on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real <BRBY>, which bid 0.47 percent stronger to 1.699 percent on the local market.\par \par \uc2 This is not far from a two-year high against the dollar, which the real hit earlier this month, and just stronger than the 1.70-per dollar level, which is deemed unofficially to be the government's comfort level.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has taken aggressive action to curb the recent rally in the real, which is making exporters' goods more expensive abroad and worsening the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 Data on Monday showed that the country's current account deficit widened by more than expected in September to $3.9 billion from a gap of $2.45 billion in the same month last year. [ID:nN25261248]\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Graphic on real:               \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par Analysis on impact:                       [ID:nN22228151]\par Recent measures in Brazil:                [ID:nN18280200]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were still trying to understand the full implications of recent measures, such as this month's tax increase on foreign bond purchases, said one head trader in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I continue to have a more tactical stance on the real, trading the extremes as the noise continues to be high," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil may also consider forcing foreign investors to pay income tax on any capital gains made from government securities as one possible way to curb inflows, local newspaper O Estado de S. Paulo newspaper reported on Monday. [ID:nN25275398]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEXICAN PESO NEAR 6-MONTH HIGH\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  <MXN=> strengthened 0.28 percent to 12.2969 per dollar, hitting its strongest level since the beginning of May.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As fears of a double-dip recession in the United States have faded, the peso has quickly recovered. As a more freely-traded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the peso also does not present any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk for investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chilean peso <CLP=>, which has been under pressure because of fears of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , firmed 0.45 percent to 484.80 per dollar. It was lifted by a rally in the price of copper, the country's main export.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jose De Gregorio said on Monday that the sharp appreciation of Chile's peso is comparable to that of other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in nominal terms. He did not signal any immediate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ID:nN25259357]\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101028e6ap001q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
