\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  rally falters after Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar recovers worldwide, curbing regional rally\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real seesaws, Chilean peso flat\par \par \uc2 * Colombia's peso falls after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rule change\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 15 (Reuters) - A recent rally in Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets ground to a halt on Friday as a stronger dollar and worries over regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave traders a good excuse to take profits.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real and Chile's peso have hit their highest levels in two years against the dollar this week on the prospect of U.S. stimulus measures, which could bring a deluge of cash into the region.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on Friday said high unemployment and low inflation point to a need for a further easing of U.S. monetary policy. [ID:nN15187998]\par \par \uc2 Easing measures could keep yields on U.S. Treasuries close to record lows and weaken the dollar, encouraging investors to borrow cheaply and pour their money into higher-yielding debt in countries such as Brazil via the so-called 'carry trade'.\par \par \uc2 But after sinking to multi-month lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the session, the dollar recovered.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> weakened as a result, but later recovered as traders also digested comments from the country's finance minister.\par \par \uc2 Guido Mantega told reporters on Friday the government was waiting for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stabilize before taking fresh measures to curb the real's rise. [ID:nN15201659]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also recently come under pressure as uncertainty has developed over the outcome of the country's presidential election. [ID:nN14103392]\par \par \uc2 Investors had previously dismissed Brazil's election as a "non-event" because ruling party candidate Dilma Rousseff looked set to sail to an easy victory, bringing few changes to current policy.\par \par \uc2 But opposition candidate Jose Serra has gradually gained in recent polls, prompting a last-minute scramble on trading floors. Serra is expected to take a tougher stance on Brazil's rallying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The way things are going, no one can now doubt that victory is apparently up for grabs, thus making the question as to how his tenure could differ from Dilma's even more relevant," said Mauricio Rosal, Latin American economist at Raymond James in Sao Paulo in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The threat of more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Colombia prompted the country's peso to weaken 0.37 percent to 1808 per dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  modified its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules, indicating it might be about to increase its dollar purchases in the market. [ID:nN15189451]\par \par \uc2 CHILEAN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SEEN UNLIKELY\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> was flat at 479 per dollar, the day after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the country's benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 2.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank has slowed the pace at which it raises rates for fear that higher rates would fuel an even bigger rally in the peso, which is trading around a 29-month high.\par \par \uc2 "The main reasons for the slower tightening pace, compared with the 50 basis point rise last time, are weak growth in developed economies posing some risks to emerging market growth", along with less concern about inflation, said Nick Chamie of \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not make as much reference to CLP strength as we would have expected suggesting that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks are still not imminent," he said.\par \par \uc2 But the threats kept coming. Chile's peso appreciation is worrying and could soon have an adverse effect on economic activity and inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Enrique Marshall said in a presentation posted on the bank's website on Friday. [ID:nN15190638]\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, U.S. stimulus measures are likely to have mixed effects on Mexico. The country sends about 80 percent of its exports to the United States, and any perceived weakness in the U.S. economy suggests reduced demand for those goods.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rate unchanged at 4.5 percent at a meeting on Friday, in an effort to boost growth.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> dropped 0.2 percent to 12.439 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101018e6af0012h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
