\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Brazil Real To Stay Strong In Short Term\b0\par\par\uc2 1,147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 16:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1419 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite continued government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real will remain strong in the short-term due to "very attractive" carry and growth trade, says Banco Santander. "A more proactive monetary approach by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Japan and increased expectations of a second round of quantitative easing by the Fed are likely to fuel riskier assets, especially the Brazilian Real..." the bank says. (Gerald.Jeffris@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1407 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD is edging closer to parity with USD for the first time since Apr, pushing USD to a fresh five-month low at 1.0011, according to CQG, as it continues to benefit from broad USD weakness. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1406 GMT [Dow Jones] Executives from \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  and \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  have launched a derivatives advisory boutique for corporate end users of derivatives, private equity firms, real estate developers and project sponsors. The Morgan execs that founded it are Joyce Frost and Frank Iacono, and the ex-SocGen founder is Chris Frost. Riverside Risk Advisors, as the new shop is known, will advise customers on structuring, pricing and executing swap transactions and structured products such as collateralized debt obligations, and where necessary help clients wind down or restructure legacy businesses. (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1406 GMT [Dow Jones] Overnight Treasury repos are normal and calm. The old 5-yr is the most costly to borrow with the lowest repo rate of 0.1%, after falling below zero last week amid a supply squeeze. The GC rate, the market's benchmark, is 0.28%, compared with zero-0.25% in the fed funds target rate. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1404 GMT [Dow Jones] Ben Bernanke should be happy. TIPS rally, extending their gains in recent weeks as buzz of QE lifts inflation expectations. The Fed minutes show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mulling options to boost inflation expectations along with more government-debt buying, which fuels more TIPS buying. The 10-year breakeven rate, a main gauge of inflation expectations, rises by 4.5 bps to 200 bps, the first time the rate hits that level since June. It signals that investors bet on an annualized inflation rate of 2% within a decade. The rate has jumped from the recent trough of 147 bps in August. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1401 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD gives back some gains as it retreats further from 1.40. Pair trading flat, at 1.3917 from 1.3914 late Tue, according to EBS via CQG. Technicals driving market now, says Flavio Giust of Key Bank. "Whereas $1.20 had been measuring level back in June, now it's $1.40." Market remains reluctant to test too wide of that level currently. USD/JPY hanging in at 81.87 up from 81.74 late Tue.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1400 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish treasury bonds weaken following higher-than-expected September CPI, to +2.5% from +2.0% in August. But traders expect the bonds to bounce back on Thursday as the market starts to realize rate hike in October is still unlikely. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.73% from 4.59% late Tuesday, 5-year at 5.14% from 5.04%, and 10-year at 5.52% from 5.44%. EUR/PLN is at 3.9484 from 3.9512 earlier Wednesday, USD/PLN at 2.8331 from 2.8259. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1354 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors are often obsessed by round numbers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and there is much discussion about AUD and CAD breaking parity, says CitiFx. "We see this obsession as misplaced since both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are largely driven by global asset market and economic conditions," it says. "Bigger surprise" will be how fast parity broken under the right scenario. The "right conditions" are a continuation of the equity and commodities rally and continued USD pressure, Citi says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1352 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds fall Wednesday, weighed by hawkish comments from ECB governing council member Weber overnight and buoyant stocks. Weber said the risks from "exiting too late" from its easy monetary stance outweighed those from "exiting too early," adding it was necessary not to defer ending non-standard measures for too long. His comments appear in sharp contrast to the Fed stance, with FOMC minutes on Tuesday hinting that quantitative easing looked increasingly likely in November. "The ECB its clearly getting the message across that it is keen to withdraw non-standard liquidity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Money market rates are expected to keep drifting higher," says a London-based trader. Earlier Wednesday, Germany sold 10-year bunds at the lowest yield ever while euro zone industrial output grew a little more than forecast. December bunds are down 0.41 at 131.60 and the 10-year bund is down at 99.80 to yield 2.273%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1351 GMT [Dow Jones] Traditional asset-allocation trades are back in style for now, featuring inverse relationship of higher stock prices and lower Tsys. "We are struck by the equity market's ability to push higher on the prospects of further [Fed] accommodation while the upside in Tsy [prices] appears to be growing tired," says David Ader, head of government bond market strategy for CRT Capital Group. Ader suggests fatigue is setting in because the market is tired of pricing in an "unknown" amount of quantitative easing. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1349 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market bonds are stronger as stocks get a boost on solid earnings. Sentiment also strengthened after FOMC minutes a day earlier indicated the likelihood of more stimulus. China's trade data is also supporting confidence. The risk premium on \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 12 bps tighter to 277 bps over Tsys. The index is up 0.33%. Brazil's benchmark bond, the Global 2040, is up 5/16 to 140 3/4 bid, according to Reuters. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] As the yen continues to appreciate, analysts expect another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . At next week's G7 meeting, Japan will try to achieve a formal permission slip for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says Adam Kritzer at forexblog.org, by arguing "'Our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't the kind of large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that aim to achieve certain rate levels over the long term.' September's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was only 'aimed at curbing excess fluctuations' in the yen's rates." Depending on how the G7 responds (via its official statement), it may influence the likelihood of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ( \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.forexblog.org/2010/10/japan-plots-next-yen-intervention.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.forexblog.org/2010/10/japan-plots-next-yen-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 .html}}}\uc2 \f2 ) [ 10-13-10 1020ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101013e6ad0009w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
