\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  has ammunition to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - finance minister\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 21:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  monitoring impact of tax on foreign investment\par \par \uc2 * May impose other measures if tax fails to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains (Recasts with quotes from finance minister, adds byline)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "a lot of ammunition" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if a recent increase in taxes on foreign investment fails to curb the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Mantega considered it too early to gauge the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of the government's decision to double to 4 percent the IOF tax on foreign investment in domestic sovereign bonds.\par \par \uc2 "At this moment we're waiting to see if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stabilize. It's possible that it happens," he told reporters at the Council of the Americas. Earlier, in a presentation to investors, he said the tax had been successful in curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains when it was introduced last year.\par \par \uc2 "If it doesn't work this time, we will be thinking about other measures," Mantega said.\par \par \uc2 He said Brazil's sovereign wealth fund is "ready to buy dollars" but hasn't done so yet because, for now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been acquiring enough dollars from the market.\par \par \uc2 Mantega, who attended the semi-annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund in Washington over the weekend, repeated his call for coordinated international action to rebalance the global economy and stop an ongoing "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war (from turning) into a trade war."\par \par \uc2 He urged strong, developed economies to resort to more fiscal stimulus rather than monetary policy to boost domestic consumption and criticized the U.S. Federal Reserve for "considering more quantitative easing" to boost the economy.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think it will reactivate the economy, but it will weaken the dollar," he said. (Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/MANTEGA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABX|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101015e6ac001gi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
