\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso plunges ahead of US jobs data\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Copper prices sink, pulling Chilean peso down 0.2 pct\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real adds 0.06 pct, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears linger\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso drops 0.7 pct ahead of U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso suffered its biggest one-day loss in over a month on Thursday as concerns about upcoming U.S. jobs data prompted investors to take profits.\par \par \uc2 The mood of caution across global markets boosted the dollar, while the rest of Latin America's major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up early gains.\par \par \uc2 Data on Friday is expected to show that U.S. nonfarm payrolls were broadly unchanged last month, suggesting the world's biggest economy continues to stagnate. For details, see [ID:nN05187700]\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> plunged 0.73 percent to 12.5688, its biggest one-day loss since Sept. 7.\par \par \uc2 "Tomorrow's data is expected to be bad -- no one wants to go to sleep with an open position," said Ramon Cordova, a trader at brokerage BASE in Monterrey, Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's markets are often hit by weak U.S. economic data due to the country's close trade links with the United States. A lower-than-expected reading of Mexico's consumer prices also piled on the pressure.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation expectations were down and this caused the peso to depreciate a bit, but (Friday's U.S.) payrolls report is the most relevant factor," said Alfredo Puig, a trader at brokerage Vector in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Traders were also looking for any excuse to take profits with the peso having rallied more than 5 percent since the beginning of September, outperforming many of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 THE GOOD, THE BAD AND THE UGLY\par \par \uc2 But a weak U.S. payrolls report also has an upside for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Speculation has mounted that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is about to inject more money into its struggling economy, prompting the dollar to weaken. [ID:nN06278713]\par \par \uc2 A worse-than-expected jobs number on Friday could further fuel that speculation, weakening the dollar and so boosting Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If it comes out weak, that raises the chance that the Fed will take measures at its next meeting, at the beginning of November," said Luciano Rostagno, the chief strategist for CM Capital Markets in Sao Paulo. But if it's strong, the dollar may briefly strengthen, he said.\par \par \uc2 However, if the number is particularly bad, causing a mass exodus from higher-risk assets, the real is also likely to weaken given its emerging-market status.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.06 percent stronger at 1.679 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market in early afternoon trading, as traders evaluated these various options.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weighed after the government this week doubled its tax on foreign purchases of bonds in an effort to curb inflows.\par \par \uc2 The stronger dollar also caused the price of copper, Chile's main export, to plunge in afternoon trading. This prompted the Chilean peso <CLP=> to reverse its gains and trade 0.19 percent weaker at 483.1 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 As in the case of Mexico, traders were also looking for opportunities to take profits on the peso which is trading at around a two year-high.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|RNP|DNP|PCO    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101010e6a7000by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
