\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Geithner: China Yuan Policy Triggering  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  War\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 17:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds Secretary comments and background.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Ian Talley \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--China's undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is triggering an international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war that risks undermining the global economic recovery, U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "When large economies with undervalued exchange rates act to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating, that encourages other countries to do the same, and this sets off a dangerous dynamic," Geithner said.\par \par \uc2 Geithner addressed two issues--exchange rates and the fiscal strategies--expected to take center stage in ministerial meetings around the International Monetary Fund's annual meeting this week and ahead of the \uc2 Group\uc2  of 20 nations summits in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Over time, more and more countries face stronger pressure to lean against the market forces pushing up the value of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the collective impact causes inflation and asset bubbles in emerging economies or else depressed consumption growth, the secretary said.\par \par \uc2 Japan, South Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  have each \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter rate strength. In the U.S., the House of Representatives has passed legislation that would slap tariffs on Chinese imports, and in Europe, the head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned that the strong euro was threatening already anemic growth there.\par \par \uc2 Without more domestic demand in surplus countries and more exchange rate flexibility, "We'll know with confidence that overall growth will be lower," the secretary said.\par \par \uc2 He said the IMF needed to play a more active role in convincing countries to float their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Geithner explicitly linked progress on governance reform--giving emerging countries a greater voice and vote at the international financial institution--to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform.\par \par \uc2 "That's the basic deal on offer," the secretary said.\par \par \uc2 But, he warned, don't look for a quick fix.\par \par \uc2 "It's not something that we're going to solve in the next three months, definitively. It's going to take a sustained set of changes over time," he said.\par \par \uc2 Reiterating a call for a measured pace out of government-led growth into tough budget-cutting periods, Geithner said most advanced economies still had room to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 While different countries face varying challenges, "concern about the near-term limits to more growth-oriented economic policies are greatly exaggerated," the Treasury Secretary said in prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 "Most of us still have the capacity to take additional actions that would improve both short-run and long-run growth prospects," and the biggest risk to the global recovery is that advanced nations underachieve on growth, Geithner said.\par \par \uc2 Although he didn't directly mention China, the secretary targeted Beijing's policy of an undervalued yuan and warned of the threat of a subsequent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 Geithner said surplus emerging-market countries with undervalued exchange rates need to also accelerate domestic demand growth.\par \par \uc2 -By Ian Talley, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9285; ian.talley@dowjones.com [ 10-06-10 1118ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101006e6a6000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
