\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Shouldn't Expect New Brazil Steps\b0\par\par\uc2 1,479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2010\par 14:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1229 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government will likely continue to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts via reverse swaps and the sovereign wealth fund to limit BRL gains, but "will not lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  battle in terms of using alternative measures," RBS Securities says. The authorities are desperate not to deflect attention to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the run-up to Sunday's presidential election, it says. "Lula wants to leave office with his 80% popularity intact and the new administration will want to use their honeymoon to attack their legislative agenda," RBS says. It is "difficult to think" that the government-backed candidate, Dilma Rousseff--who holds a commanding lead in polls--would raise taxes on foreign short-term investment, as it would "deflect initial confidence away from what is likely to be a pragmatic reform agenda based on regulatory and bureaucratic reform in order to increase investments (foreign and domestic) to meet Brazil's large infrastructure gap," RBS says. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1230 GMT [Dow Jones] The Institute for Supply Management-New York's Current Business Conditions index increased to 58.3 this month from 55.6 in August. The report also showed businesses lifting their expectations into 2011, with Six-Month Outlook index jumping to 64.8 from 58.4. But some signs of inflation: The Prices Paid index jumped to 53.3 from 43.2 in August. The report said the price index is at its highest in two years.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1226 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD at 1.3658, USD/JPY at 83.30, GBP/USD at 1.5883 ahead of real 2Q GDP figures and weekly jobless claims at 8:30am ET. Numbers, including later Chicago PMI, will likely set tone for investors seeking clarity on possible coming QE2. USD expected to remain under pressure all day. "A surprise to the upside [on jobless claims] would be consistent with increased downside pressure on U.S. front-end rates and thus on USD/JPY," say \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1220 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys start higher in NY Thursday, reversing Wednesday's losses. Month-end, quarter-end buying bolsters demand. Fed is scheduled to buy long-dated maturities in midmorning. Final estimate of Q2 GDP and weekly jobless claims are due 8:30 a.m. EDT. 10-yr is 7/32 higher to yield 2.474% and the 30-yr bond is 15/32 higher to yield 3.659%.(min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1219 GMT [Dow Jones] Dollar down against the majors ahead of fresh U.S. data Thu, which will likely set tone for investors seeking clarity on possible coming QE2. Real 2Q GDP figures and weekly jobless claims at 8:30am ET. EUR clinging to $1.36 level with investors less perturbed by stresses in euro zone. USD/JPY hit overnight new post-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  low of Y83.16. UK pound rose to a high of $1.5923, a mark last seen in Aug, after reported increase in third-quarter credit availability.(andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1207 GMT [Dow Jones] EUROPEAN SUMMARY: After a shaky start the euro comes out on top Thursday while the dollar is weak across the board. European government bonds tread water and European equity bourses trade negatively. EUR/USD printed the day's low of 1.3559 in the wake of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  one notch downgrade of Spain's credit rating to Aa1 and news that the Irish government's bailout of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anglo Irish Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  could reach EUR34B. However, in what looks like 'sell the rumor, buy the fact' the euro started to climb, picked up a little speed after German September jobless dropped by 40K instead of the 20K expected and then surged on news that demand at the ECB's 6 day tender slumped to EUR29.3B against forecasts of some EUR70B. EUR/USD is rushing to a fresh 5-month high of $1.3676, while USD/CHF sank to a fresh 30-month low of 0.9708 and GBP/USD gained over one cent to a fresh 7-week high of 1.5923. The latter no doubt helped by comments from BOE's Posen that he could be talked out of voting for more QE and a small, but positive 0.1% gain in the Nationwide September house price survey. USD/JPY slipped ever closer to BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  territory basing out at 83.16, its lowest level since the Sept. 15 BOJ action which has been confirmed at Y2.12T making it the biggest one day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  total ever. Away from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  European government bonds end the session close to flat as peripheral euro-zone concerns were offset by easing banking-system worries after the ECB 6 day tender and narrowing yield spreads. December bunds are up 0.01 at 131.82 while December gilts are down 0.02 at 124.69. The main European bourses are down between 0.3% and 0.9%, gold hit another all-time high of $1315oz while oil managed a 7 week high close to $79bbl. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1204 GMT [Dow Jones] Whereas other central banks are moving to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in their local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will remain hands-off for the time being, \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. "The hurdle for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is a moving target and not a line in the sand...the peso is far from the type of misalignment that justified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past," the investment bank added. It sees the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moving towards market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the peso continues to firm to CLP445 to CLP450, compared to many other analysts' estimates of a CLP460-470 range. Exporters have been clamouring for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the stronger peso hurts the competitiveness of their products. The peso ended unchanged Wednesday, just shy of a 27-month high, at 485.50 to the dollar. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1200 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed lower Wednesday at 0.408% versus Tuesday's 0.425%. Thursday, the interbank overnight rate is trading higher between 0.40% and 0.70%. A money dealer says with regard to the wide range that "the market is very chaotic at the moment," pointing to the end of a one-year tender. Earlier Thursday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.892% vs 0.886% Wednesday. (herbert.rude@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1144 GMT [Dow Jones] Rising food prices in Brazil shouldn't affect consumer price inflation unless it turns into "significantly high and protracted food inflation," says RBS Securities. The inflation of manufactured goods at the wholesale level is likely to remain tame, anchored by low inflation abroad and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, RBS says. "Still, for the time being, given that food inflation is on a rise and is unlikely to moderate anytime soon, we should be prepared for adverse inflation surprises in the upcoming weeks," RBS says. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1130 GMT [Dow Jones] Calif gov race very close with Democrat Jerry Brown (37%) and Republican Meg Whitman (38%) in a virtual tie among likely voters, with 18% undecided, a survey from Public Policy Institute of Calif. says. In U.S. Senate race, incumbent Barbara Boxer leads Republican Carly Fiorina 42%-35%, with 17% undecided. Despite declaration that national recession is over, 89% of residents say Calif is in recession, and 62% say jobs and economy are most important issue. Approval ratings of state and federal elected officials at or near record lows, PPIC said, and only 45% are satisfied with choice of candidates in governor's race. (stan.rosenberg@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1056 GMT [Dow Jones] The U.S. data slate is beginning to get exciting, notes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The week's most important data release, the ISM index is just a day away but beforehand comes today's Chicago PMI index at 1345 GMT, which acts as a leading indicator for the former, albeit a poor indicator. Other data of note Thursday are the 2Q GDP revision and initial jobless claims at 1230 GMT. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the same applies to all three data releases: only notable positive surprises will prevent the Fed from QE2. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1039 GMT [Dow Jones] The prospect of weak euro zone peripheral PMIs on Friday and an offered USD/JPY suggests significant risk of a downside correction in EUR/JPY says \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Now at 113.85 the bank says a break below the 112.85 support area could be the trigger for such a move. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) [ 09-30-10 0830ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100930e69u0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
