\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Brazil public accounts struggle, inflation jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 21:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's primary budget surplus below expectations\par \par \uc2 * Overall budget deficit widens in August from year ago\par \par \uc2 * Broad measure of inflation jumps in September\par \par \uc2 By Ana Nicolaci da Costa and Isabel Versiani\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Sept 29 (Reuters) - Growth in Brazil's economy stoked inflation in September but the jump in activity wasn't enough to prevent a deterioration in public accounts, data showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil posted a lower-than-expected primary budget surplus in August. The surplus remained far below the government's target as a percentage of gross domestic product, despite record tax collection.\par \par \uc2 While growth of around 9 percent annually in Brazil has generated robust tax receipts, this has not been enough to offset the surge in government spending ahead of Oct. 3 national elections.\par \par \uc2 The government still expects to achieve its primary budget target of 3.3 percent of GDP in 2010, by possibly excluding spending for its flagship infrastructure program from the primary budget tally.\par \par \uc2 A massive capitalization of oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  should also help inflate primary surplus numbers in September, Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say the primary surplus may become less relevant to track the government's ability to meet debt payments as the overall budget shows a bulging nominal deficit and signs of deteriorating public accounts.\par \par \uc2 "The government is managing to do a lot of maneuvering in the public accounts to try to achieve the primary surplus (target)," Luiz Eduardo Portella, partner at Banco Modal in Sao Paulo said.\par \par \uc2 Runaway government spending worries investors partly because it can be inflationary by stimulating an economy that is already growing briskly. It also can push up borrowing costs in an economy that already suffers from some of the world's highest interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The consolidated primary budget surplus <BRPSPS=ECI>, which excludes interest payments, edged higher to 5.2 billion reais ($3.1 billion) in August from 5.04 billion reais a year earlier. It was below the 6 billion reais expected in the median forecast of 11 analysts surveyed by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The surplus in the 12 months to August dipped to 2.01 percent of GDP from 2.02 percent in the year to July and stayed far below the government's 3.3 percent target for all of 2010.\par \par \uc2 The primary surplus "is no longer a good thermometer. (Brazil's) gross debt does not stop rising while the net debt is stable, but every one looks at the gross debt," Portella added.\par \par \uc2 RISING DEBT\par \par \uc2 Brazil's net public debt to GDP <BRDGDP=ECI> stood stable from July at 41.4 percent, while the gross debt eased slightly to 59.4 percent of GDP in August from 59.6 percent of GDP in July. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected it to rise to 60.4 percent of GDP in September, Altamir Lopes, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic research department told reporters in Brasilia.\par \par \uc2 Analysts also fear that the country's debt burden could increase if Brazil's finance ministry decides to use the sovereign wealth fund to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Treasury has issued some 18 billion reais of bonds to capitalize the sovereign fund and could sell more debt as Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  has said there is no limit to size of the fund's potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The country's overall budget deficit <BRBUD=ECI> widened to 10.5 billion reais from 8.2 billion reais in August last year.\par \par \uc2 Growth in the labor and credit markets are some of the signs that economic activity is regaining momentum and filtering into inflation numbers.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's broadest inflation measure surged 1.15 percent in September, from 0.77 percent in August, data from the Fundacao Getulio Vargas on Wednesday showed. See [ID:nN29240232].\par \par \uc2 The IGP-M is closely monitored by analysts and investors because it provides a broad look at wholesale and consumer prices in Latin America's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The numbers, along with rising inflation expectations and data last week showing consumer prices rose more than expected in the month to mid-September, help reinforce expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to resume monetary tightening in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "We will have more pressure on inflation this semester, there is no way around it," Andre Perfeito, an economist at Gradual Investimentos in Sao Paulo said.\par \par \uc2 ($1=1.704 reais)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Luciana Lopez in Sao Paulo; Editing by Andrea Ricci)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100929e69t001cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
