\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real gains despite threats; peso firms\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gains despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso firms 0.2 percent on Fed hopes\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso strengthens for fourth straight session\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments about Brazil's real, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/BRAZIL, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's real strengthened on Monday despite fresh efforts by the government to talk down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect the country's struggling exporters.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's finance minister said the country still has an arsenal of measures to stop the real strengthening during an "international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" in which governments are manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost export competitiveness. See[ID:nN27256208]\par \par \uc2 But traders have gradually become used to hearing such threats, which have yet to be followed up by concrete action.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> bid 0.06 percent stronger at 1.708 reais on the local spot market after the warnings.\par \par \uc2 A record-breaking stock sale from state oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  has prompted investors to pour money into Brazil over the past few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Since buyers must hand over their cash for the shares on Wednesday this week, Monday is the last day when foreign investors will bring their dollars into the country because it takes about 48 hours to make a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 It's possible Mantega's comments were just "a conditional threat he hopes not to have to act upon," said Tony Volpon, head of emerging market research for the Americas at Nomura Securities.\par \par \uc2 Even if the government does take further measures, it is likely they are "waiting for both the \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  transaction to close and next Sunday's presidential election to pass before acting," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso extended gains on Monday, also boosted by the weaker dollar which sent investors looking for higher-yielding assets in Latin America.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=><MEX01> strengthened 0.19 percent to 12.526 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to record its largest gains in the month of September in 28 years according to Mexican bank Banamex.\par \par \uc2 EYES ON FED\par \par \uc2 Investors are betting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will boost money supply to aid economic recovery in the United States, Mexico's most important trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect the Fed will keep interest rates near zero through 2011 and could even increase its purchases of U.S. bonds, which would also help keep yields down on Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 The expectation of lower yields on U.S. Treasuries has prompted a rally in higher-yielding Latin American assets.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders said the peso's rapid acceleration could slow later in the session as U.S. stock markets edged lower.\par \par \uc2 "Last week's gains were helped by a strong performance in the stock markets, but the peso's acceleration is going to pause a bit as markets are a bit sluggish on renewed concerns about the health of European banks," said Ramon Cordova, a trader at brokerage BASE in Monterrey, Mexico. .\par \par \uc2 The euro earlier dipped after ratings firm \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cut \uc2 Anglo Irish Bank\uc2 's lower-grade debt and kept it on review for a downgrade, a move that highlighted concerns over the euro zone banking sector. [ID:nN27338134]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed for the fourth straight session, gaining 0.25 percent to 485.3 per dollar and closing at its strongest level since June 2008. A weaker dollar, booming growth, and strong demand for Chile's copper exports have boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over recent months.\par \par \uc2 Lower yields in the United States have also prompted investors to venture into some of the most inhospitable parts of Latin America's capital markets, such as Venezuelan debt.\par \par \uc2 Prices for Venezuela's benchmark bonds due in 2027 <VENGLB27=RR> were boosted further on Monday as investors bet that opposition gains in Sunday's parliamentary elections might temper the behavior of President Hugo Chavez. [ID:nN27245671]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100930e69r001du\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
