\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico, Chile pesos firm on bets Fed could ease\b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 23:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso firms 0.55 pct; \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real drops 0.17 pct\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed as real edges closer to key 1.70 level\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso hits 8-month high as copper rallies (Adds comments from Mexico, Chile; updates prices to close)\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso strengthened sharply to a five-week high on Wednesday as markets braced for more monetary easing from the U.S. Federal Reserve.\par \par \uc2 The Fed suggested on Tuesday it could pump more money into the American economy, where investors remain concerned about the possibility of a second recession.\par \par \uc2 That resolve to keep the U.S. economy buoyant eased investors' nerves, making relatively risky Latin American assets more attractive, said Raphael Martello, an analyst with Tendencias consultancy in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso <MXN=> firmed 0.57 percent to 12.6372 per dollar, hitting its strongest intraday level since Aug. 19. Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also strengthened, which bolstered the price of its top export, copper.\par \par \uc2 "When you know the world is not going to end, investors start moving toward this carry trade and they buy (Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Martello said.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts suggested Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appealed to investors because the peso is more fairly priced than its Latin American counterparts.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Latin America have been on a tear lately and, with the notable exception of the Mexican peso, most are now trading above what might reasonably deemed to be fair value," Capital Economics said in a report.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  PLANS\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> weakened 0.17 percent to 1.719 reais per dollar as traders grew cautious about more aggressive moves by the country's authorities to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rally.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will carry out any dollar purchases made by the country's sovereign wealth fund in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Even though no concrete measures were announced, the comments were enough to scare some investors into selling reais.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also stepped up its dollar purchases in the spot market. Data released on Wednesday showed the bank has recently been buying as much as $1 billion a day. [ID:nN22239158]\par \par \uc2 Expectations of huge foreign investment in an upcoming share offering by state-controlled oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  have caused the real to strengthen more than 5 percent since the end of June.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.85 percent on Wednesday to an 8-month high against the dollar. Chilean President Sebastian Pinera said on Wednesday there is not an immediate need for government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow its recent ascent. [ID:nN22256063] (Additional reporting by Manuela Badawy in New York; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100925e69m000db\par }\