\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Weakens Slightly As Market Debates  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 15:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real switched course and weakened slightly against the dollar Tuesday as a debate raged in the markets over whether or not the government will step up measures to try to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Dollars have been flowing into Brazil attracted by strong growth, high domestic interest rates and plenty of investment opportunities, including an upcoming mammoth share issuance by the government-run oil company, \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2  (PBR), or \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government has become ever more concerned about the impact of a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the rest of the economy, with exporters in particular feeling much of the pain, and officials have talked about taking steps to dent demand for the real.\par \par \uc2 In the latest announcement, late on Monday, the government said it has allowed Brazil's sovereign wealth fund to buy up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market. The government said there's no limit on how much the fund can use of its reserves, which are estimated at around BRL18 billion.\par \par \uc2 In addition, there is speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may start holding three auctions to buy dollars per day, instead of two, and that it might resort to reverse-swap auctions, in which investors exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions for government debt linked to interest rates, to dampen demand for reals.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday morning, the real was trading at BRL1.7300 per dollar on the B&MFBovespa exchange in Sao Paulo, slightly weaker than Monday's close of BRL1.7292.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are divided over whether, or when, the government will actually take any steps. Some believe they won't be able to combat the longer-term appreciation trend; others believe the government may wait for an appropriate moment to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RBS Securites in a note said the government may choose to hold back some of its firepower until after the \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  share issuance is out of the way later this month. \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  is looking to raise some $20-25 billion from capital markets, and a large share of that is expected to come from overseas investors buying up locally-issued shares, which has driven up demand for the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Banco Santander is skeptical that the Brazilian government will take any drastic action, and sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  testing the BRL1.7 mark in the short term.\par \par \uc2 "Although the technical positioning seems less favorable for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have reached another level, we still believe that strong dollar inflows and the lure of the carry and growth trades will prove formidable obstacles against real depreciation in the short term," Santander said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the cost to the Brazilian government of buying dollars is rising, given the widening gap between interest rates in the U.S. and Brazil, said \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in a note. Brazil issues bonds to finance its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases; this is contributing to its growing budget deficit, which reached an eight-month high in July, BBH said. At the same time, growth differentials and strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contribute to the yawning current account deficit, which is approaching record levels, it said.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 21-09-10 1311GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100921e69l0010h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
