\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso flirts with four-week high\b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2010\par 16:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Investors optimistic about Tuesday's U.S. Fed meeting\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.1 pct, Mexican peso gains 0.3 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's markets closed for a public holiday (Recasts; adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Noe Torres\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - The Mexican peso hovered around a four-week high against the dollar Monday as investors grew optimistic about Tuesday's U.S. Federal Reserve meeting.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers in the United States are unlikely to announce new monetary policy moves, but some analysts expect them to give a slightly more optimistic outlook for the economic growth.\par \par \uc2 That would be good news for Mexico. While Brazil sells vast amounts of its exports to China, Mexico relies almost entirely on trade with its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 Fears earlier this year of a double-dip recession in the United States hit the peso hard. But as those concerns have faded, the peso has begun to outperform the region.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened 0.28 percent to 12.7695 per dollar Monday, just shy of its strongest level since Aug. 23.\par \par \uc2 "It's possible that tomorrow, with more data indicating a deceleration instead of a recession, the Fed will show it's a bit more optimistic in general," said IXE economist Luis Flores in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was bid 0.06 percent stronger at 1.716 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market, not far from its strongest level this year.\par \par \uc2 Flores said there was also a cautious mood across trading floors due to the prospect of more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Foreign interest in the country's debt and optimism over high growth rates have helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to double in value against the U.S. dollar since 2003.\par \par \uc2 "What is making the real gain strength against the dollar is not what is usually referred to as speculation, it's more of a fundamental shift," said Andre Perfeito, an economist at Gradual Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 PESO OPTIMISM SPREADING\par \par \uc2 The upcoming inclusion in October of Mexican debt in a major global bond index (WGBI) run by \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  is also supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The Mexican peso continues to recover well, likely aided by inflows associated with the imminent inclusion into the WGBI," said Clyde Wardle, an emerging markets analyst at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , in a research note.\par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , which has expressed some of the most optimistic views about the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently among international banks, advised clients to bet that the peso could strengthen to as much as 12.55 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 RBC analysts also look set to join the bullish camp. "Risk reversals suggest that positioning in the Mexican peso has increased sharply in recent weeks and it may soon be worth expressing a bullish Mexican peso view as a relative value trade," they wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 Markets were closed in Chile for Independence Day celebrations. (Additional reporting by Caroline Stauffer in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100923e69k000zh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pic