\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  c.bank to step up  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 -report\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hold several surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions\par \par \uc2 * Measures may also include sale of reverse swaps\par \par \uc2 * Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted more \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  action\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely intensify its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  with surprise daily auctions to buy excess dollars in the spot market, up from just two now, O Estado de S. Paulo newspaper reported on Friday, citing an unnamed government source.\par \par \uc2 "The order is to buy, buy and buy," the government source told Estado.\par \par \uc2 The more aggressive measures could also include the sale of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps if investors continue to raise short bets against the dollar in futures markets, Estado said.\par \par \uc2 The focus on a more hard-line \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach was an answer to the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday that totaled an estimated $21 billion, Estado said, citing comments from the Brazilian government source.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, <BRBY><BRL=> has rallied nearly 5 percent since the end of June, making the country's exports less competitive in global markets and also stoking demand for imports.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been holding one auction a day for several months, but last week began calling two daily auctions to buy dollars in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a bid to soak up large volumes of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flowing into Brazil. The bank has bought $815 million in the spot market so far in September, including almost $600 million over Thursday and Friday last week, according to its most recent data. (Reporting by Elzio Barreto; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|D|M|RNP|DNP|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100917e69h000rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
