\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Gains Ground But  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Linger\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened slightly against the dollar on Friday, wrapping up a week in which the fear of greater government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stalled the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong gains.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian government had been unable to do much to prevent the real from gaining ground on Monday and Tuesday, despite increasingly strong comments from Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hold twice-daily auctions to buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 But an unusual move on Wednesday by the Japanese government to weaken the yen changed the dynamic in global markets, and the real slipped sharply. Since then, the real recovered some poise but didn't get return to test what traders see as the next barrier of BRL1.70.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL1.7165 Friday on the BM&FBovespa exchange, slightly stronger from Thursday's close. The real gained about 0.7% against the dollar this week, and is about 2.3% stronger against the dollar since the beginning of the month.\par \par \uc2 The real has been driven by the booming economy and strong appetite for investments in Brazil, but that has been compounded in recent weeks as companies issue bonds overseas and repatriate the proceeds. Investors have also been jockeying for position as state-owned oil company \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2  (PBR), or \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , embarks on a mammoth share issuance which is expected to wrap up later this month.\par \par \uc2 Many overseas investors are expected to participate in the share issuance, in which the Brazilian company is looking to raise roughly $25 billion from the private-sector capital markets.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, there was more evidence on Friday of the government's desire to capitalize on the doubts that have crept into investors' minds in recent sessions. Estado reported Friday that the order at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to "buy, buy, buy" dollars, to absorb the strong inflows and prevent an excessive appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Every day this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held two auctions to buy dollars, ostensibly to build its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but markets are also keenly aware that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to influence the market's perceptions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves rose by $4.8 billion between Monday and Thursday, evidence of the stepped-up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the total amount rising to $267.2 billion as of Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government this week again promised to do what it can to absorb the dollars flowing into the economy.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to soak up any excess dollars that might come in with the \uc2 Petrobras\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mantega said. "I'm giving advance warning; we're going to buy it all."\par \par \uc2 The strong appreciation hurt exports, reducing Brazil's trade surplus and feeding a rising current account deficit. The country's year-to-date trade surplus totaled $11.981 billion through mid-September, compared with $20.678 billion in the same period of 2009.\par \par \uc2 There's also some speculation that the government may use so-called reverse-swap auctions, which it has used in the past to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. In a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap, investors exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions for government paper linked to interest rates. The auctions typically help support the U.S. dollar against the real by removing real exposure from the futures market.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 17-09-10 2016GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100917e69h00156\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
