\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Gains Vs Dollar, But  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Doubts Linger\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 14:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gained some ground against the dollar Thursday morning, but there's hesitation in the air amid expectations that the Brazilian government may step into the market at any moment to try to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The market is very much going to turn on expectations as to whether or not the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will or won't carry out a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, of Fourtrade Corretora de Cambio in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  has stressed in recent days that the government has the firepower to be able to absorb the flood of dollars coming into the local market, largely due to heavy overseas bond issuance by Brazilian companies and an upcoming huge share issuing by oil giant \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2  (PBR), or \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market had largely shrugged off that talk until Wednesday, when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese government to prevent the yen from gaining too much against the dollar led to a global reassessment of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions. The Brazilian real ended six straight sessions of gains against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the real was trading at BRL1.7225 on the B&MFBovespa exchange, slightly stronger than Wednesday's close of BRL1.7258.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually warns the market the day before it plans to carry out the swaps, Baldan said.\par \par \uc2 In a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap, investors exchange foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions for government paper linked to interest rates. The auctions, which were held on a near-daily basis in 2005 and 2006, typically help support the U.S. dollar against the real by removing real exposure from the market.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 16-09-10 1258GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100916e69g00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
