\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real off; Colombia peso down on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  plan\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 17:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Colombian peso falls 1 pct on cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan\par \par \uc2 * Weak U.S. manufacturing data prompts regional losses\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real down 0.4 pct; Chilean peso drops 0.2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso strengthens 0.4 pct ahead of holiday (Adds Mexico commentary, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Nelson Bocanegra and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA/MEXICO CITY, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Colombia's peso fell sharply on Wednesday after authorities said they would buy dollars to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally while Brazil's real weakened after worse-than-expected U.S. manufacturing data.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost 0.95 percent after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would start purchasing at least $20 million daily for the next four months.\par \par \uc2 "Those who were short dollars yesterday had to exit to buy at whatever price," said Camilo Perez, chief economist at \uc2 Banco de Bogota\uc2  in the country's capital.\par \par \uc2 Investment in Colombia's booming oil and mining sectors has led the Colombian peso to strengthen more than 10 percent this year, putting pressure on the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2 Across the rest of the region, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly sagged after a surprise drop in manufacturing activity in New York state during September. [ID:nN15143494]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> shed 0.4 percent to 1.716 on the local spot market after the U.S. data, while Chile's peso <CLP=> weakened 0.18 percent to 494.60 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latin America, a major producer of commodities and manufactured goods, would suffer should the global economy take a turn for the worse.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed 0.37 percent to 12.7759 per dollar ahead of a two-day holiday that begins on Thursday. The peso has been supported in recent weeks by Mexico's scheduled entry into \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's WGBI World Bond Index on October 1, which could boost flows into Latin America's second largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Regarding Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its exchange market, analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures will knock up to 2 percent off the peso in the near-term.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, some analysts said the bank could not hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 "These types of actions can't change a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term tendency," Correval economist Daniel Velandia wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 JAPANESE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Japan's decision on Wednesday to sell yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in six years fueled debate about how the measure might affect Brazil's real.\par \par \uc2 One head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at an international bank in New York said the move could prompt Japanese retail investors, who already have some of the biggest bets on the real's appreciation, to sink more money into the real.\par \par \uc2 "Retail (investors) will look at this spike as a good opportunity to add," he said.\par \par \uc2 That might put pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts in the market to protect exporters.\par \par \uc2 But other market players were less convinced.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think they will add much more to the position," said Pedro Tuesta, an economist at 4Cast in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners already hold near-record bets on the future appreciation of the real, so Japan's move is unlikely to prompt a huge shift into Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. [ID:nTOE68E02W] (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo; Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100918e69f0009i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
