\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real tests cenbank, region firms\b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 15:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * U.S. retail data raises hopes about global recovery\par \par \uc2 * Chile and Mexican pesos gain 0.2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Brazilian real pulls back from 2010 high (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real hit a fresh 2010 high on Tuesday as investors bet on massive future investment in Latin America's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 Strong U.S. retail data also helped to boost the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing the Mexican peso to shrug off early losses. [ID:nN14247794]\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRL=> edged up 0.018 percent from the previous day's close to bid 1.7092 reais per U.S. dollar, according to the international reference rate. Earlier in the session it closed at 1.703 on the local spot market <BRBY> -- its strongest level since Dec. 4, 2009.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- in a bid to protect exporters -- but it has so far failed to halt the real's rally\par \par \uc2 "The market is testing the government's willingness and they will continue to take the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower," said one head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in New York.\par \par \uc2 Brazil announced on Tuesday plans to sell $500 million more of its 2041 global bond, underscoring a growing foreign interest in the country's markets.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also optimistic about huge foreign investment in an upcoming fund-raising deal by state-owned oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  and a wave of other local corporate deals.\par \par \uc2 But if the real breaks the closely-watched 1.70 per dollar level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be forced to take more aggressive action in the market, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Authorities have already been increasing their dollar purchases in the spot market, calling multiple auctions each day, but some believe they may also start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market via derivatives called 'reverse swaps'.\par \par \uc2 PESO HOSTAGE TO U.S.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> gained 0.21 percent to 12.8277 per dollar, hitting a three-week high, after the strong U.S. data raised hopes about the global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's fragile recovery from a deep recession is especially dependent on U.S. growth because Mexico sends about 80 percent of its exports over its northern border.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico's peso in particular among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain hostage to what happens in the United States," Roberto Melzi, a Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York said.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> gained 0.24 percent to 493.3 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, recouped early losses.\par \par \uc2 "In Chile, the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a scenario of rising risk appetite and rates normalization will continue to push the Chilean peso higher," said analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100917e69e000zq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png