\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  firms, defying cenbank\b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 22:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Strong U.S. data on jobless claims boosts region\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.1 pct, Mexican peso gains 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Yields on Brazil rates fall on inflation slowdown (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Jean Luis Arce\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Brazil's real firmed on Thursday, defying attempts by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect local exporters.\par \par \uc2 Euphoria over booming foreign investment in Latin America's biggest economy has recently boosted the real, lifting it last week to its strongest level against the U.S. dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 After seesawing on Thursday, the real <BRBY> closed 0.12 percent stronger at 1.721 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market. It was boosted by a rally among the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following stronger U.S. jobs data that increased appetite for riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Investors boosted the real despite the decision by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on both Wednesday and Thursday by calling more than one auction to buy U.S. dollars. For details, see [ID:nN08128231]\par \par \uc2 Traders expect a massive share offering by state-owned oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , planned for later this month, to lure $15 billion to $25 billion of foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 The capitalization plan will not be the only deal to boost the real, Marjorie Hernandez, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York, said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 "The fulfillment of \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 ' capitalization will also unclog the domestic capital markets pipeline, opening the door for other M&A deals in the latter part of the year," she said.\par \par \uc2 The bank changed its forecast for the Brazilian real to 1.70 in the third quarter and 1.74 in the fourth quarter, from a previous forecast of 1.84 for both quarters.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, the Mexican peso <MXN=> strengthened 0.48 percent to 12.9900 per dollar after new U.S. claims for unemployment benefits fell more than expected last week to their lowest level in two months. [ID:nN09174403]\par \par \uc2 Mexico's fragile growth is dependent on the economic recovery of the United States since the country sends about 80 percent of its exports over its northern border.\par \par \uc2 "This good data got rid of the bad sentiment which has been accumulating in the last month and this is supporting the peso," said Ramon Cordova, a trader at brokerage BASE in Monterrey, Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.1 percent to 496.2 per dollar. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points to 2.5 percent at its Sept. 16 monetary policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 SLOWER BRAZIL INFLATION SURPRISES AGAIN\par \par \uc2 Yields fell on Brazilian interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> following data showing slower-than-expected inflation for August. [ID:nSPG003039]\par \par \uc2 Investors bet the data would put less pressure on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the cost of borrowing over coming months.\par \par \uc2 At the beginning of this month, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its benchmark interest rate at 10.75 percent, ending a monetary tightening cycle that helped cool a red-hot economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also released the minutes from that meeting on Thursday, showing it is not currently concerned about a possible sharp rise in the cost of consumer goods.\par \par \uc2 However, some economists believe that rising food prices next year will force the bank to revise its view and increase borrowing costs again.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the contract due January 2012 <DIJF2>, one of the most heavily traded contracts of the early session, fell to 11.27 percent from 11.36 percent. (Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100912e699000e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
