\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil says will not let real overvalue\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 22:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Brazil will take measures to avoid real appreciating\par \par \uc2  * Latest sign govt ramping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market  (Adds debentures comment last paragraph)\par \par \uc2  RECIFE, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 9 (Reuters) - Brazil's government on Thursday said it would take necessary steps to stop excessive appreciation of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , marking the latest sign it is ramping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  is gearing up for what markets expect to be large inflows attracted by a massive stock offering from oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2  "We will take the necessary measures to prevent that there be an excessive appreciation (of the real)," Mantega said in a speech at an event in the northeastern city of Recife.\par \par \uc2  He made the comments after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called its second auction on Thursday to buy U.S. dollars on the spot market.\par \par \uc2  The bank has stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after the real firmed 4.7 percent against the dollar since the end of June, putting pressure on the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2  Brazil's economy has been among the best performers in the world this year. Mantega said he expected the economy to continue to grow at a sustainable pace.\par \par \uc2  He saw average annual growth of 5.8 percent in coming years, after expansion of more than 7 percent in 2010.\par \par \uc2  A challenge for the next government following Oct. 3 elections will be to keep the current account balanced and keep investment compatible with the country's needs, he added.\par \par \uc2  The government was studying tax breaks to help stimulate growth of the domestic debentures market, Mantega said without giving further detail.\par \par \uc2  (Reporting by Bruna Serra; Writing by Ana Nicolaci da Costa; Editing by Andrew Hay)    \par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100909e699001el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
