\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rally tests cenbank, region mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 16:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * U.S. jobs, housing and manufacturing data boosts region\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real firms 0.7 pct, Mexican peso adds 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso 0.1 pct weaker as banks buy cheap dollars (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 2 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real extended its rally on Thursday after the government confirmed a long-awaited oil fundraising plan which should lure a huge amount of money to Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The gains put more pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect exporters, whose goods have become increasingly expensive abroad as a result of the real's rally.\par \par \uc2 Optimism over the U.S. economic recovery after a rush of strong employment, manufacturing and housing data over the past two days, also boosted the rest of Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> bid 0.74 percent stronger at 1.732 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market -- the third straight day of gains, taking the real to a fresh four-month high.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of speculation, Brazil's government finally set the price it will charge state-owned oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  for crude reserves to be used in a $43 billion oil-for-shares swap. [ID:nN01187399]\par \par \uc2 The announcement put an end to recent uncertainty and boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the biggest effect really is the confirmation of the capitalization. This is what is giving most support to the real, even though it's now under this support level of 1.75 (reais per dollar)," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist for the CM Capital Markets brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT\par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains stronger than 1.75 reais against the dollar for an extended period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could try to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, analysts had said.\par \par \uc2 But now some believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could only take new measures once the 1.70 real-per-dollar level is broken.\par \par \uc2 Verbal warnings, bigger or multiple U.S. dollar purchases and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market via so-called reverse swaps are the most likely options. [ID:nN23213114]\par \par \uc2 "It is a near-term risk; either that they buy dollars more aggressively or possibly resume those \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverse swap auctions as we approach 1.70," said Paul Biszko, a strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to act before the key U.S. monthly payrolls report on Friday, which could have a big impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> edged 0.1 percent higher to 13.0560 per dollar following the strong U.S. data which raised hopes about the recovery of Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 However, investors were cautious ahead of the payrolls report.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened 0.1 percent to 497 per dollar after hitting its strongest level in more than seven months, as the price of copper, the country's main export, rose. [ID:nLDE6810SN]\par \par \uc2 Traders in Santiago said banks took advantage of the early rally to buy dollars at a relatively cheap level.\par \par \uc2 YIELDS FALL AFTER BRAZIL RATE HELD\par \par \uc2 Yields fell on Brazilian interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the benchmark interest rate at 10.75 percent late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Although the decision had been widely expected, the bank also signaled that there was little chance of further rate hikes in the months ahead. [ID:nN01111893]\par \par \uc2 "We retain our view of protracted pause of the monetary policy as long as commodities prices remain well behaved," said analysts at RBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 However, they said yields were also falling after sharp gains on Wednesday following strong manufacturing data from China and the United States.\par \par \uc2 The interest rate futures market in Brazil tends to react just as much to the changing outlook for global growth as it does to national interest rate expectations, they noted.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the contract due January 2012 <DIJF2>, one of the most heavily traded contracts of the early session, fell to 11.29 percent from 11.37 percent.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero and Molly Rosbach in Santiago; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100905e6920008t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
