\par\par \b \uc2 SCENARIOS-Brazil weighs options to halt real's rise\b0\par\par\uc2 885 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2010\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 24 (Reuters) - Compared to the rest of Latin America, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an old pro at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Haunted by memories of rampant inflation in the 1980s and 90s, Brazil's authorities have continued to play an active role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, primarily through U.S. dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 But the real soared 34 percent against the greenback last year, putting a huge pressure on the country's exporters. Investors flocked to Brazil in the aftermath of the financial crisis since it was one of the few places offering high interest rates and returns, and thus big profits.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened so far this year, fund-raising plans by local companies and renewed interest in Brazilian bonds has caused the real to firm 2 percent since June, prompting the government to consider getting tougher.\par \par \uc2 Following are measures which Brazil's authorities have used before and could use again to curb the real's appreciation:\par \par \uc2 * VERBAL WARNINGS\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is adamant that it is not trying to secure the real at a specific level.\par \par \uc2 But that has not stopped economists and traders from fixating on 1.75 as the maximum value the real could be allowed to strengthen against the U.S. dollar before the government takes more aggressive action.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's finance minister, Guido Mantega, has frequently issued cautionary comments about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. Further warnings should be expected whenever this level is broken for more than a few days, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 * BIGGER OR MULTIPLE DOLLAR AUCTIONS\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already been increasing its dollar purchases in the spot market via daily auctions, which it resumed on a regular basis in May 2009.\par \par \uc2 But despite almost doubling its purchases so far this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to test the 1.75 level.\par \par \uc2 Analysts argue that the auctions are also creating a guaranteed market for dollars in Brazil which could actually cause the real to strengthen in the long-term.\par \par \uc2 One temporary option would be to call more than one auction on the same day, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last did in May this year.\par \par \uc2 By changing their routine, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would "wrong-foot" the market, sending a stronger signal to traders without necessarily buying more dollars, said Mike Moran, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in New York.\par \par \uc2 * SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUND PURCHASES\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Treasury has also been buying more dollars, making the most of cheap greenbacks to pay off foreign debt, but the effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been minimal.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's sovereign wealth fund, which was authorized last December to buy dollars but has yet to do so, could also be used to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2 However, after the initial shock to the market, this strategy faces the same pitfalls as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily auctions, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 * REVERSE \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  SWAP AUCTIONS\par \par \uc2 "Below 1.70 they would probably pull out the big guns, such as reverse swaps," says Kathryn Rooney Vera, an emerging markets strategist at Bulltick Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps are derivatives which, when auctioned to the market, would have the same effect as buying U.S. dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used them regularly between February 2005 and September 2008, and has recently considered reintroducing them, ringing up dealers last month to gauge demand.\par \par \uc2 While the auctions represent a warning to the market about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, they do not actually weaken the real on a technical level. Under the swap contract, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pays out the interbank lending rate on a set amount of reais in exchange for a fixed rate in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Their use did not stop the real strengthening to 1.56 in July 2008 from 2.60 reais in February.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  analysts argue that the government is also reluctant to use derivatives because, unlike dollar purchases which are ostensibly made to accumulate reserves or pay off debts, swaps would be seen as a direct attempt to manipulate the market.\par \par \uc2 * CAPITAL INFLOWS TAX INCREASE\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge last year prompted the government in October to slap a 2 percent tax on foreign purchases of stocks and bonds to curb inflows and contain the real's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 This tax could be increased if the real decisively breaks below the 1.70 level, say analysts at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But such a policy change could be more tricky in the next few months given the country's upcoming presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 Aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be even more unlikely if \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling party candidate and election favorite, Dilma Rousseff, wins, says Miriam Tavares, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at the AGK brokerage in Sao Paulo. She believes opposition candidate Jose Serra would make more of an effort to curb the real's rise in an effort to boost exports.\par \par \uc2 However, the scope and scale of these various measures will ultimately depend on events abroad, says Win Thin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If we continue to get weak numbers of out of the United States and continue to see emerging markets weaken, then these policymakers are off the hook." (Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/ (SCENARIOS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100824e68o000m1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
