\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on Fed, China worries\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2010\par 15:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Slowdown in Chinese demand adds pressure to region\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso weakens 0.7 pct, Brazil's real dips 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Investors eye Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as real nears 1.75 (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Tuesday as cautious investors ditched higher-risk assets worldwide ahead of the outcome of the Federal Reserve's policy meeting later in the day.\par \par \uc2 If the Fed does not announce any further measures to boost the U.S. economy, as many expect it to do, the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other riskier investments could suffer, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's statement is expected to be released at around 1815 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over slowing demand from China, which buys the majority of Brazilian exports, also weighed on the region.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government's self-induced slowdown caused imports to grow less than expected in July, according to data released on Tuesday. For details, see [ID:nTOE67904G].\par \par \uc2 "Several subtle data points emerged overnight confirming a recent cooling in overall economic activity and had the effect of washing out those who had feasted on a growing risk appetite during recent sessions," said Andrew Wilkinson, senior analyst at Interactive Brokers in Greenwich, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.46 percent weaker at 1.758 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market in mid-session trading.\par \par \uc2 If the negative mood in global markets persists, the real is likely to trade between 1.76 and 1.77 per dollar on Tuesday, Miriam Tavares, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at brokerage AGK Corretora in Sao Paulo, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 But if investors' appetite returns following the Fed statement, any local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains could be limited by the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCB), she added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers last month to gauge their demand for a possible offering of so-called reverse swaps -- a form of derivative which would allow the bank to effectively buy U.S. dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 "Fresh inflows and the return of foreign capital to the stock market in the past few days, as well as the improving trade balance, is reinforcing expectations of a stronger real," she said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  noted on Tuesday that investors in Brazil are increasingly shifting from bond purchases to stocks. [ID:nN10139757]\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to adopt a more aggressive approach, whether it be via the auction purchases in the spot market or bringing up the issue of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps again, if it wants to secure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 1.75 per-dollar level," AGK's Tavares said.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> weakened 0.65 percent to 12.7010 per dollar. The Mexican economy is heavily dependent on U.S. growth since the country sends about 80 percent of its exports to its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 Data on Tuesday showing an unexpected drop in U.S. non-farm productivity in the second quarter, the first decline since late 2008, made investors even more cautious.\par \par \uc2 A sharp slowdown in U.S. activity would also reduce the amount of money Mexican workers in the United States send to their families back home.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened 0.16 percent to 512.30 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, fell ahead of the Fed statement. ( Editing by W Simon )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100813e68a0010e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
