\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real slips as IP drop feeds rate view\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 16:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real slips as investors curb rate hike bets\par \par \uc2 * Third month of falling IP shows Brazil is cooling\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  delay speculation also weighs on real\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's peso slips, Chile's peso gains on China news (Recasts; adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Aug 3 (Reuters) - Brazil's real led Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' losses on Tuesday after a drop in industrial production fed expectations that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not hike interest rates as much as expected.\par \par \uc2 Pressuring Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board, weak U.S. data highlighted the slackening pace of growth in the United States, one of the region's top trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real saw the biggest losses after data showed industrial production dropped 1 percent in June from May, marking the third straight month of declines as Latin America's largest economy cools from booming growth earlier in the year. For details, see [ID:nN03274323]\par \par \uc2 A spate of weaker data in Brazil has pushed investors to pare back expectations for interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 "That is putting a little bit of a headwind into the appreciation of the real, along with the increased talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jorge Perez-Duarte, managing director of emerging markets at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 The real had gained more than 2 percent from a mid-July low before Tuesday's losses.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the real strengthens much past the 1.75 per dollar level. On Tuesday, the real <BRBY> bid 0.46 percent weaker at 1.757 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 WEAK U.S. DATA\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> seesawed after the industrial production data left investors unsure about whether Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to raise rates at its next meeting.\par \par \uc2 Yields first dipped, before rising as market players who have bet on less-steep hikes took profits on recent gains, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Bets on further rate hikes in Brazil have fallen sharply in the last month.\par \par \uc2 The market is currently pricing in only a 50 percent chance of a 25 basis point hike at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next policy decision, due September 1, said Tony Volpon, head of Americas emerging market research at Nomura Securities in New York.\par \par \uc2 The market has also been cutting back expectations of further hikes next year.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of people are backtracking furiously, and that is not good for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Volpon said.\par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the real was market chatter about a further delay of an up to $25 billion share offering by \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , Brazil's state-controlled oil company. \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  reaffirmed on Monday a previously reported September deadline, but doubts lingered about that timeframe. [ID:nN02111873]\par \par \uc2 "It is not clear what is going to happen but any postponement or noise can affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that is already positioned to absorb part of this deal," a New York-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 Weighing on sentiment across the region, data showed U.S. factory orders fell steeply in June while an index of pending home sales plunged to a record low in the same month. Data on U.S. personal income and spending in June was unexpectedly flat.\par \par \uc2 U.S. growth, which is largely driven by consumer spending, is vital for Latin America's own economic health since the region exports huge amounts of agricultural and mineral goods to the United States.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> weakened 0.13 percent to 12.5905 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> bid 0.27 percent stronger to 516.50 per dollar after Chile's state miner Codelco , the world's top copper producer, said China's plan to bring electricity to rural areas would demand one million tonnes of copper in the next two and a half years.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100806e683001rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
