\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Closes Weaker On Possible Action By  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, facing resistance after hitting its strongest level in months Monday, on expectations of more aggressive market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL1.7587 to the dollar, weaker than Monday's close at BRL1.7500.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the real weakened on market ideas that any strengthening beyond the psychological barrier of BRL1.75 to the dollar could prompt more aggressive Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the real briefly traded between BRL1.74 and BRL1.75, closing at BRL1.7500 on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given signals that it could resume what are known as reverse swap auctions to prop up the U.S. dollar. Traders said these rumors have a greater effect in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the real strengthens toward BRL1.75 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The reverse swap auction is a form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market. At the auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps contracts indexed to interest rates for futures contracts linked to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.\par \par \uc2 Such auctions are a way to relieve pressure against the dollar by eliminating short-dollar positions. Traders said Brazilian banks and funds have accumulated sizeable short-dollar positions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest in supporting the dollar is based on the fact that Brazilian exporters lose revenue and market share when the real is strong.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the dollar bucked the prevalent global trend. In international trading, the dollar closed lower against the euro and Japanese yen on a string of weak U.S. economic figures and indications from the U.S. Federal Reserve that it could engage in another round of monetary easing to aid the sluggish U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, global metals prices were mostly lower on the uptick in global risk aversion, but oil prices closed higher. Prices in the commodities are important supports for the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , determining export revenue for Brazilian commodities producers.\par \par \uc2 On Brazilian credit markets, short-term interest-rate futures contracts were mostly higher Tuesday, as investors expected industrial production to pick up speed in July and August after data released Tuesday showed a decline in June.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded interest-rate futures contract on the Brazilian Financial Exchange, that of January 2012, rose to 11.58% after closing Monday at 11.51%.\par \par \uc2 -By Todd Martinez, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7082; brazil@dowjones.com [ 03-08-10 2034GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100803e683001gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
