\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real breaks key level,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2010\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real breaks 1.75 level, eyes on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * European bank earnings, US factory survey data support\par \par \uc2 * Colombia peso hits 9-1/2 month high against dollar\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Aug 2 (Reuters) - Brazil's real hit a three-month high on Monday despite the threat of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also jumped on solid European bank earnings and U.S. factory data.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso <COP=STFX> hit a nine-month high while Mexico's peso <MXN=> traded at its strongest in six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Strong financial results from Europe's banking sector and data showing the U.S. manufacturing sector grew in July for the 12th straight month gave investors greater confidence in the strength of global economic recovery. [ID:nN02183874]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has gained around 3 percent from a mid-July low. Mexico's peso has risen close to 5 percent from its weakest level seen early last month.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said thin, summer trading was exaggerating recent gains.\par \par \uc2 "We have come a long way on these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  without much volume. I would be cautious that people would be willing to take profits on these moves rather quickly," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities in Stamford, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> broke through the closely-watched level of 1.75 per dollar to bid 0.46 percent firmer at 1.746 per dollar in the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 Speculation has mounted that piercing the 1.75 level could push the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market to tame the real's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The market is testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve," said Cattan-Naslausky.\par \par \uc2 LOW-VOLUME GAINS\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors enamored with Brazil's growth prospects have gobbled up local assets and driven the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to double in value against the dollar since President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva took office in 2003.\par \par \uc2 The flow of dollars into Brazil has strengthened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  enough to put significant pressure on exporters' profit margins.\par \par \uc2 Local authorities are already using a capital inflows tax and daily dollar purchases in the spot market to break the tide. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to wade into the derivatives market soon, where most foreign market players are making their big bets.\par \par \uc2 Cattan-Naslausky doubted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts amid a low volume move of the real.\par \par \uc2 "The flows are not there, so coming in with this strategy to absorb flows doesn't make much sense, it would only sharpen volatility," she added.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed 0.49 percent to 12.5745 per U.S. dollar as the U.S. manufacturing survey boded well for further recovery in Mexico's closely-linked factories.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <> firmed 0.66 percent to 517.70 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, traded at three-month highs. [ID:nLDE6710PA]\par \par \uc2 Oil prices and higher commodity prices support Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general, given the region's big output in goods like Mexican oil and Brazil's iron ore and soy.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.67 percent to 1,832 per dollar, pulling back slightly after hitting its strongest since mid-October 2009.\par \par \uc2 Yield spreads between emerging market bonds and U.S. Treasuries, a key gauge of risk aversion, narrowed 17 basis points to 270 basis points, according to the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  EMBI+ index <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's benchmark 10-year peso bond <MX10YT=RR> bid down to a fresh all-time low early in the session, but pared back to bid down 1 basis point at 6.52 percent.\par \par \uc2 Mexican bonds have rallied this year as Europe's debt crisis put a shine on Mexico's relatively trim fiscal deficit and market players also bet on big flows later this year when \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  will include peso debt in a major index.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100805e682001ht\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
