\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on U.S. consumer mood\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2010\par 18:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister tips possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real loses 0.41 pct, Mexico peso slides 0.15 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chiles peso knocked off three-month high\par \par \uc2 (New throughout, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, July 27 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on Tuesday, hurt by a drop in U.S. consumer confidence, and Brazil's real lost ground after the country's finance minister backed further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso hit its highest level in over a month early in the session and Chile's peso traded at a three-month high before lackluster stock markets pushed investors to cash in on recent gains in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Confidence among American consumers dropped in July to the lowest level since February on worries about the job market, the Conference Board reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "There are a lot of mixed signals out there, such as talk of deflationary pressures but then you see good earnings reports," said Jorge Perez-Duarte, managing director of emerging markets at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen a good rally in the last few days, so it is a bit of a technical rebound as people take some profits," Perez-Duarte said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has advanced 3 percent from a low on July 2, while the real has gained more than 2 percent since June 29.\par \par \uc2 Concerns have eased about a financial crisis in Europe following stress tests of banks, while solid revenue outlooks from some bellwether companies like \uc2 FedEx\uc2  have offset fears the U.S. economy is slowing.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=><MEX01> slipped 0.15 percent to 12.6895 per U.S. dollar while the Brazilian real <BRL=> bid 0.41 percent weaker in international trade to 1.7688 per dollar. Chile's peso <CLP=CL> shed 0.19 percent to 519.70 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL JAWBONING\par \par \uc2 Brazil's finance minister Guido Mantega on Tuesday voiced his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. [ID:nN2798713]\par \par \uc2 Speculation is mounting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step up measures to contain the real's strength, which is hurting exporters. The bank itself informally sounded out demand for reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps last week.\par \par \uc2 But analysts were skeptical that new measures would have much more success than a capital inflow tax and daily dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 "I do not think verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be enough, because even actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been enough," Perez-Duarte said.\par \par \uc2 Investors will continue to demand Brazilian assets due to the country's prospects for growth and some of the highest yields among investment-grade emerging markets, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil launched $750 million worth of reopened 2021 global bonds on Tuesday, more than the $500 million initially offered, as the deal found strong demand among investors, Thomson Reuters' IFR reported. [ID:nN27184714]\par \par \uc2 Yield spreads between emerging market bonds and U.S. Treasuries, a key gauge of risk aversion, narrowed 10 basis points to 273 basis points on Tuesday, according to the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  EMBI+ index <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 The country risk spread on Brazilian bonds fell 7 basis points to 198 basis points, trading at its narrowest since the middle of May. (Editing by Eric Walsh)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100730e67r0021t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
