\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm after U.S. data\b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2010\par 15:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real under pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans\par \par \uc2 * Strong U.S. new home sales data boosts region\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso firms 0.2 pct, Brazil's market split (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, July 26 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Monday after data showed U.S. sales of new homes surged in June, restoring some confidence in the recovery of the world's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 But Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were mixed due to expectations that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may shift its involvement in the market.\par \par \uc2 Fears over a fresh slowdown in U.S. growth have hit Mexico particularly badly since the country sells about 80 percent of its exports to its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 But data on Monday showing that sales of new, single-family homes rebounded in June sent Mexico's peso to its strongest level in more than a week. For details, see [ID:nN26203473]\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> firmed 0.24 percent to 12.700 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The sales data came in above what was expected and by a lot, so this is giving a little more certainty to the outlook," said Omar Martin del Campo, a trader at Banco Ve Por Mas in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> edged 0.17 percent stronger to 519.10 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, touched a 10-week high. [ID:nLDE66P0SW]\par \par \uc2 But traders were cautious after the Chilean peso clocked its biggest weekly gain since May on Friday, due to the expectation of greater dollar inflows as the state moves to cash in its copper revenues.\par \par \uc2 According to the international reference rate, the Brazilian real <BRL=> was 0.34 percent stronger at 1.7675, buoyed by the strong U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 REVERSE SWAPS DIVIDE BRAZIL'S MARKET\par \par \uc2 But on the local spot market, the real <BRBY> was 0.57 percent weaker at 1.768 compared to Friday's closing level.\par \par \uc2 Traders attributed the difference to chatter about a possible shift in the way \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "Late last Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil (BCB) 'checked' with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer desks the demand for 'reverse swaps'," said Tony Volpon, Latin America strategist with Nomura Securities.\par \par \uc2 Reverse swaps are a form of derivative that would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take a long position in the U.S. dollar futures market in exchange for a short position in the interest rate markets.\par \par \uc2 Selling reverse swaps would be a way to reduce the arbitrage opportunities in the market, which have arisen due to the huge reserves the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has amassed through daily U.S. dollar auctions.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  informally consulted the market around 1740 local time on Friday, according to one trader, causing the international reference rate to weaken sharply in late trading.\par \par \uc2 But by that point, the local spot market in Sao Paulo had already closed for the day. As such, Friday's closing level on the local spot market was much stronger than the international reference rate, meaning that Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were compared against widely different bases.\par \par \uc2 The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered reverse swaps was in September 2008.\par \par \uc2 "In fact it is a bit of a mystery why the BCB is not doing this already if its implicit goal is to depreciate or dampen the Brazilian real," Nomura's Volpon said.\par \par \uc2 However, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reluctant to use derivatives as a tool for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of their lack of transparency, wrote analysts at \uc2 J.P.Morgan\uc2  in a note earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The real also pared gains after Brazil's current account deficit for June came in far worse than expected compared to the year-ago period. Imports jumped faster than exports and companies sent more money abroad. [ID:nN26154475]\par \par \uc2 "But the current account deterioration has been going on for some time now," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities. The expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume reverse swaps was exerting a bigger pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo and Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 (samantha.pearson@thomsonreuters.com; Reuters Messaging: samantha.pearson.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net; +5511-5644-7736)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100729e67q001i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
