\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil justifies  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  action on 'flash-crash' Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 By Walter Brandimarte   \par \uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2010\par 00:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, May 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars on May 6, the day the U.S. stockmarket briefly plunged, in order to absorb excess greenback inflows and to avoid alarming investors in a day of heightened market anxiety, the bank's president said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks suddenly crashed on Thursday May 6, with the Dow Jones <.DJI> recording its largest-ever intraday point drop in a span of about 20 minutes, when the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its usual auction to purchase dollars in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 That decision was "absolutely" in accordance to the government policy of mopping up excess dollar liquidity, regardless of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Henrique Meirelles said.\par \par \uc2 "If you look at that period you'll observe that (dollar) flows were positive. They were actually extremely positive that day," Meirelles told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show a net inflow of $2.24 billion into Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on May 6, more than twice the level of the previous day, as exporters took advantage of a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring their dollars into the country.\par \par \uc2 Meirelles claimed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction didn't add volatility to the market either, as the real trimmed losses of about 5.0 percent later in the day to close about 3 percent weaker.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action also aimed at transmitting a sense of normalcy to investors, he said.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had unnecessarily suspended the auction in a day of highly positive dollar inflows, that could have caused volatility in the market," Meirelles said.\par \par \uc2 "Investors would wonder what is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can see see and they can not."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on a daily basis, expect during holidays, since early May 2009, when it revived its strategy to boost foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 It had halted those auctions after the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  in 2008, when global aversion to risk soared and dollars started flowing out of the country.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -MEIRELLES/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100518e65i001ka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
