\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2010\par 21:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the second-consecutive session.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL1.7370 to the dollar on Brazil's BM&FBovespa exchange, weaker from Thursday's close at BRL1.7302.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded stronger throughout the session as expectations for heavy foreign-investment inflows increased in the wake of Wednesday's decision by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked the benchmark Selic base interest rate by 75 basis points to 9.5%. The bank is also expected to front-load a series of rate hikes aimed at controlling inflationary pressures and avoiding an overheated economy, according to economists.\par \par \uc2 Higher interest rates in Brazil typically attract heavy foreign inflows from investors seeking better rates of return. Brazil has been a favored destination for carry trade players, who borrow cheap cash overseas and invest in Brazil.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets also appeared to dismiss threats made by Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin, who said Thursday that the treasury was prepared to start buying dollars to counter any steep appreciation in the real. Traders said that until the treasury actually started buying dollars, the threat lacked credibility.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, was more than willing to back up the threat. For the second-consecutive session, the bank held two spot-market dollar purchase auctions. The bank bought an undisclosed volume of dollars at BRL1.7312 and BRL1.7342 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The auctions followed a similar move during Thursday's session, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have purchased nearly $1.5 billion on the spot market, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy hand was significant because the real was also getting a boost from market players holding short-dollar positions ahead of Friday's Ptax, traders said. The Ptax is the average daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate used to settle futures contracts, and will be used to settle futures contracts Monday.\par \par \uc2 The typical month-end tug-of-war between short- and long-position holders adds a dose of volatility to trading each month. The timing of two-consecutive double auctions during the heat of the Ptax battle was significant--and shows the bank is serious about undercutting the real, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The bank has held a single daily purchase auction since May 2009. Before this month, the last double auction was held in 2007--with the more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting on April 15, when the bank held its first double auction.\par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures contracts also reflected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate hike and expectations for future hikes.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded contract, January 2011, rose to 11.12% after closing Thursday at 11.01%. The contracts reflect investor expectations for average annual interest rates at future dates.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's overnight interbank lending rate, known as the CDI, was even with Thursday's close at 9.36%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's benchmark Global 40 bond was flat at a bid of 133 7/8.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085, Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 30-04-10 1935GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100430e64u001tk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
