\par\par \b \uc2 LATIN AMERICAN MARKETS: Brazil's Bovespa Falls As \uc2 Net Servicos\uc2  Slumps\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carla Mozee  \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2010\par 02:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's key equity index fell Thursday, with telecommunications stocks and cable operator \uc2 Net Servicos\uc2  struggling with losses after a broker downgrade of the Latin American telecom and media sector.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Bovespa fell 0.7% to 70,524.35, with only consumer discretionary and pulp and paper stocks among the few issues that moved higher. \uc2 Fibria Celulose\uc2  (FBR) led advancers for a second straight session by rising 3.4%, and packaging producer Klabin (KLBAY) rose 1.3%.\par \par \uc2 But decliners were led by a 4.1% slump in \uc2 Net Servicos\uc2  (NETCD) shares after \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  downgraded its rating on the company to neutral from buy, saying the cable operator is "approaching the natural limits of its network," and facing strong competition from satellite TV operators.\par \par \uc2 "We also are concerned about potential corporate-governance issues, as Brazil moves to pass a law that will allow the Carlos Slim group to take over NET," analyst Stephen Graham wrote in a note to clients. Goldman also took \uc2 Net Servicos\uc2  off of its Focus list.\par \par \uc2 The broker downgraded its view on the region's telecom and media sector to a cautious view from neutral. "As a defensive sector, telcos should continue to lag equity markets as appetite for risk continues to rise and as the economies of LatAm bounce back," wrote Graham.\par \par \uc2 Goldman said it will focus on "pure mobile operators" \uc2 Vivo Participacoes\uc2  (VIV) and \uc2 TIM Brasil\uc2  (TSU), as they are fully exposed to "still-growing wireless demand in Brazil and should capture (and drive) mobile-data growth."\par \par \uc2 Shares of Vivo fell 2.2% and TIM finished unchanged at 4.79 reals ($2.73). Oi (TNE) also declined, by 0.2%. But \uc2 Brasil Telecom\uc2  (BTM) outperformed the group with a rise of 2.9%\par \par \uc2 As part of its sector assessment, the broker downgraded \uc2 NII Holdings\uc2  (NIHD) to neutral from buy. \uc2 Telecom Argentina\uc2  (TEO) was upgraded to neutral from sell, and fixed-line company \uc2 Telesp\uc2 , which operates in the state of Sao Paulo, was reinstated as neutral as the company "pays healthy dividends and trades below its historical average multiple."\par \par \uc2 Telecom Argentina\uc2  shares rose 0.9%, outperforming Argentina's Merval index, which fell 0.8% to 2,461.83.\par \par \uc2 Investors in the Brazilian equity market on Thursday appeared to have set aside data showing that China's economy expanded 11.9% in the first quarter from the year-earlier period, exceeding analyst expectations. China became Brazil's biggest trading partner last year.\par \par \uc2 In Brasilia Thursday, Brazil President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and China President Hu Jintao signed a four-year bilateral action plan as well as a number of separate agreements aimed in part at strengthening their trade ties.\par \par \uc2 Hu had to cut short his tour of Latin America, however, to return to China to deal with the aftermath of an earthquake that struck the Qinghai province on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversed earlier advances and finished lower against the greenback after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to buy dollars. It was the first time since 2007 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held two auctions in one day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined 0.3% to 1.754 reals per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "becoming more aggressive within its key objective of stemming the pace of BRL appreciation," as it faces the prospect of strong inflows based, in part, on renewed interest in IPO deals and the start of the rate-tightening cycle later this month, wrote RBS Securities \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Flavia Cattan-Naslausky in a clients' note.\par \par \uc2 The real had gained ground earlier in the session after reports on monthly employment and consumer prices bolstered the widely held view that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise the benchmark interest rate when it releases its decision April 28. The key rate now stands at 8.75%. [ 04-15-10 2017ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020100416e64g00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
