\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  cenbank brakes  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  strength, not for long\b0\par\par\uc2 808 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2010\par 17:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Double \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lays floor for the dollar\par \par \uc2 * Purchases haven't halted real's appreciation in the past\par \par \uc2 * Positive inflows to continue in the short term\par \par \uc2 By Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, April 16 (Reuters) - Stepped-up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should brake the real's appreciation as traders mull what other government actions could be on tap.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say strong dollar inflows over the next few weeks will eventually cause the real <BRBY> to strengthen anew.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday held two auctions to buy dollars on the spot market -- the first time it did so since July 13, 2007.\par \par \uc2 The back-to-back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the real had firmed 4.63 percent over the previous 12 sessions. Inflows into Brazil, a darling of foreign investors, as well as higher investor appetite for risk amid waning fears of a Greek default were seen factoring into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb.\par \par \uc2 That kind of appreciation is worrying to Brazil, Latin America's largest economy and a recent magnet for inflows.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to have a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, trying to brake things a bit," Ilan Goldfajn, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director and current chief economist for \uc2 Itau Unibanco\uc2 , said on Thursday, hours before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the markets.\par \par \uc2 "If there's more exchange rate pressure, we'll see action from the sovereign wealth fund to try to hold the line," he added.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has occasionally even sold dollars, it has steadily been a buyer of dollars since last May as Brazil's swift rebound from the global economic crisis saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  begin its steady advance.\par \par \uc2 In 2009, the real surged 34 percent against the dollar, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases.\par \par \uc2 The government slapped taxes on inflows into local stocks and bonds in October, and on American Depositary Receipts in November, in an effort to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains as Brazil's exporters wrung their hands over the sudden relative increase in expense for their products.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has no exchange rate target, and that the dollar purchases are geared to boosting Brazil's international reserves, already above $245 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Perhaps in the next days or hours, investors will have some wariness about being long on the real," said Cristiano Oliveira, chief economist with Banco Safra de Investimento.\par \par \uc2 Tony Volpon, a strategist with Nomura Securities in New York, also saw a cause for the effect in the market.\par \par \uc2 "A second auction on the same day is a clear signal (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is not happy with current levels. Market is right to react," he wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 But the bank could also be preempting heavier inflows coming soon, said Nathan Blanche, a partner at Tendencias consultancy in Sao Paulo, especially in light of the 10-year bond launched by Brazil on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions give the market a new reference point, Blanche said.\par \par \uc2 "Some traders could see this as a floor signaled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they're mistaken. It's an uphill battle for any government to try to establish an exchange rate ... they would have to change policy," he said.\par \par \uc2 EFFECT BACKFIRING\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to weaken the real, Safra's Oliveira said the effect will not last long.\par \par \uc2 "All the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to do is buy dollars -- or speed up the pace of buying -- and the real, days later, gains even more. We've seen this before," he said, referring to 2008.\par \par \uc2 Among the transactions likely to bring in dollars soon are a share offering from \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  , Latin America's largest bank by assets, which hopes to sell another 286 million shares. At Thursday's close of 30.90 reais, that would bring in around 8.8 billion reais.\par \par \uc2 Later, the capitalization of state-controlled oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , which could range from $20 billion to $50 billion.\par \par \uc2 Sidnei Nehme, executive director of the NGO brokerage, has argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases could backfire.\par \par \uc2 The auctions add to reason for financial institutions to bring in resources from abroad, safe in the knowledge that the government will soak up those inflows, he said.\par \par \uc2 At the start of the year, the Treasury's threat to buy dollars through the Sovereign Wealth Fund kept the real above 1.8 per dollar for more than a month.\par \par \uc2 But in the wake of the Treasury's recent silence, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resumed its climb.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the real dipped 0.17 percent to 1.752 per dollar. Before the second auction, the real traded 0.74 percent firmer at 1.736 per dollar -- its strongest since January.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100416e64g001au\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
