\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil plans no  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  changes on inflation-report\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2010\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from stoking inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles said in an interview with the \uc2 O Estado de Sao Paulo\uc2  newspaper published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> surged 34 percent in 2009, making it among the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar last year, but it has tumbled 5.6 percent so far in 2010, raising concerns that rising import prices may pressure consumer prices.\par \par \uc2 Meirelles said the exchange rate is only one of several components that may affect inflation and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate setting committee, known as Copom, considers all of the factors when deciding on borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 "We have a target for inflation, not for the exchange rate," Meirelles said in the Estado interview. "We don't make a decision on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of inflation."\par \par \uc2 Dollar inflows to Brazil have dropped in February after "substantial" volumes in January, but Meirelles said that decline was normal and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to purchase greenbacks on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Meirelles told Estado he would have no qualms in hiking the benchmark Selic interest rate this year despite national elections in October, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bases its decisions on macroeconomic models and projections.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Elzio Barreto; editing by Stuart Grudgings and W Simon )\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100210e62a001be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
