\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks close higher, led by Vale; real dips\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2010\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks closed up on Tuesday in choppy early trading, following overseas equities higher.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index <.BVSP> advanced 0.73 percent to 69,908.59 for its second straight gain.\par \par \uc2 The advances mirrored U.S. stocks' rise, which were led broadly higher by healthcare shares and \uc2 McDonald's Corp\uc2  , which was upgraded by \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . [ID:nN19231844]\par \par \uc2 "The market has been very volatile. The turnaround was confirmed when (the U.S. market) opened abroad," an equities trader in Sao Paulo said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, weakened 0.34 percent to 1.774 per U.S. dollar. The real lost ground last week on increased bets the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign wealth fund.\par \par \uc2 "We stick to our 1.800 (real) target, also sustained by a more favorable scenario for the USD globally," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  noted in a report Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In the Bovespa mining company Vale , the world's largest producer of iron ore and second most heavily weighted stock in the index, led gains, rising 1.18 percent to 47.25 reais.\par \par \uc2 Also climbing were shares of aircraft maker Embraer , which moved up 4.9 percent to 10.07 reais. The company could see an uptick in business from \uc2 Japan Airlines Corp\uc2  as the bankrupt carrier rejigs its fleet toward smaller and more fuel-efficient aircraft. [ID:nTOE60I0B1]\par \par \uc2 Pulp and paper company Fibria added to its gains of the previous sessions by another 4.52 percent to 38.15 reais. Those shares had plunged 10.5 percent over four days before turning positive on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Limiting gains were shares of state-controlled energy company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , which slid 0.47 percent to 36.38 reais as crude oil <CLc1> saw choppy trading but ultimately settled higher on Wall Street gains. [ID:nN19234153]\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures contracts <0#DIJ:> broadly, though not uniformly, edged higher.\par \par \uc2 Investors use the contracts to bet on trends in the country's benchmark interest rate, the Selic, currently at a record-low 8.75 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers meet next week to consider changes to the rate. Analysts generally expect policymakers to keep the rate steady through that meeting, with the Selic to increase at some point in 2010.\par \par \uc2 But there is little consensus on when those hikes could begin. (Reporting by Ana Nicolaci da Costa and Luciana Lopez; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100119e61j001we\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
