\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  c.bank to step up  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 -report\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2009\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ease the appreciation in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, the country's largest newspaper reported on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles told President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva that purchasing U.S. dollars on the spot market had limited effect on the exchange rate, but that the bank would intensify its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term, Folha de S.Paulo newspaper said, without citing a source for the information.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought nearly $9 billion on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since early May to soak up greenbacks pouring into the economy and prevent further appreciation of the real. Manufacturers and agribusiness leaders have called on the government to do more as a strong real hurts their overseas sales.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened 27.2 percent against the dollar so far in 2009 and is up nearly 33 percent since reaching a three-month low in early March, reducing the competitiveness of Brazilian exports abroad.\par \par \uc2 Meirelles also told Lula that there is room for the bank to lower benchmark borrowing costs further, though any declines would be limited, Folha reported. The bank cut the so-called Selic rate by 50 basis points in July to an all-time low of 8.75 percent. (Reporting by Elzio Barreto; Editing by Theodore d'Afflisio)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090813e58d0010g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
