\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Ends 3.0% Weaker At BRL2.442 Per Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 20:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real dropped sharply to end 3% weaker against the dollar Monday as concerns over the health of major global financial sector players and a continuing decline in key commodities prices prompted investors to dump the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.442 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange after ending at BRL2.3695 per dollar Friday.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered from the outset of the session under the weight of global risk aversion raised by weak fourth-quarter results from major international financial sector players.\par \par \uc2 Top among those was insurer \uc2 American International Group Inc\uc2 . (AIG), which posted a record loss of $61.66 billion in the fourth quarter. The result prompted the U.S. government to offer additional assistance to the company of near $30 billion.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the signs of trouble was \uc2 HSBC Holdings PLC\uc2 's (HBC) report of a 70% decline in profits in 2008 to $5.7 billion. That result forced the bank to cut dividend estimates and close a number of consumer lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in North America.\par \par \uc2 Compounding the effect of that news was further disappointing economic data abroad. Early in the session, the Euro Zone and the U.K. both reported record lows in their February manufacturing indices and both Italy and Canada reported sharp economic contractions in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Alongside those factors were a steep decline in commodities prices, including oil and metals. Those price declines, analysts note, could have an adverse impact on Brazil's trade balance, which has already been negatively affected this year by diminished global demand.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a dollar sale auction, strengthening market perceptions that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seek a natural equilibrium point as the global economy continues to adjust to an ongoing slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Despite the recent weakening of the real, market participants continued to show some belief the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stage a recovery through the end of the year. According to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weekly market survey released Monday, the real is seen strengthening to around BRL2.30 per dollar by the end of 2009. According to the same survey, the country's reference Selic interest rate is seen falling through the end of the year to 10.25% annually from a current 12.75%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in local rate futures trading Monday, rates on the most heavily traded contract, January 2010, rose to 10.66% from 10.63% at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's interbank overnight rate held steady at 12.62%.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 02-03-09 2004GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090302e532000tf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
