\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  drop on U.S. data, banks\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2009\par 16:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Wednesday after weak retail data in the United States and a grim outlook for banks renewed concerns about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo stock exchange sank 3.95 percent to 37,981.77 points, nearly wiping out all of this year's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The mood is much worse... all the news is really bad," said Alberto Dwec, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at \uc2 Souza Barros\uc2  brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Sales at U.S. retailers dropped 2.7 percent in December, suggesting the recession has the potential to be the longest and deepest since 1981.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of more losses ahead for banks also took a toll on equity markets, dragging down major U.S. indexes. Brazilian markets followed suit.\par \par \uc2 Financials were hammered hard, with Bradesco shedding 6.04 percent to 21.01 reais, while Itau closed 7.52 percent lower at 24.36 reais. Unibanco slumped 7.74 percent to 13.58 reais and \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  fell 6.74 percent to 14.11 reais.\par \par \uc2 Energy and commodity shares also had a bad day.\par \par \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , the heaviest weighted stock in the Bovespa index, slid 2.71 percent to 23.30 reais, while mining company Vale fell 3.93 percent to 25.70 reais.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Brazilian real <BRBY> closed at 2.349 per dollar, a loss of 0.95 percent from Tuesday's close. The real has shed more than 3 percent of its value in the last three sessions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to help add liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling an unspecified amount of dollars on the spot market. It also sold a total of $1.276 billion in dollar repurchase agreements in two separate auctions.\par \par \uc2 The most liquid interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> contract rose slightly after a few days of declines. The yield on contracts to January 2010 closed at 11.56 percent, while the January 2012 ended at 11.75 percent. (Reporting by Aluisio Alves and Jennifer Correa; Writing by Renato Andrade, Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090114e51e0018c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
