\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Early On Commodities, Overseas Mkts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2009\par 12:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened against the dollar in early trading Monday under the effects of falling commodities prices and declining markets overseas.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.297 per dollar after ending at BRL2.271 on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Friday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seeing the impact of a generalized decline in commodities prices in the wake of falling demand.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices on the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2  were down about 5% in early trading Monday, falling below the $39 per barrel mark.\par \par \uc2 The lower oil prices brought a knock-on effect to metals and other key commodities of which Brazil is a major exporter.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, traders noted investment inflows to Brazil have been weakened over recent sessions, tracking declines in overseas markets.\par \par \uc2 Further weakening the real, meanwhile, were growing expectations Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cut interest rates more sharply than initially forecast at a monetary policy meeting scheduled for later in the month.\par \par \uc2 The bank is now seen cutting the rate by as much as three quarters of a percentage point from a current 13.75% annually in reaction to slowing domestic demand and decelerating inflation. Earlier projections had called for a half-point rate cut.\par \par \uc2 The bank is next scheduled to review its rate stance on Jan. 21.\par \par \uc2 Falling interest rates locally often discourage dollar inflows locally as investors seek out more elevated returns abroad.\par \par \uc2 To provide for liquidity and curb excessive volatility, meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen possibly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday with a spot market dollar sale. The bank has sold dollars from foreign reserves regularly at daily auctions since September to limit volatility.\par \par \uc2 According to a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released Monday, the real is seen weakening to around BRL2.30 per dollar by the 2009 from a projection of BRL2.25 per dollar seen earlier.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has fallen about 30% against the dollar since August in reaction to investor risk aversion prompted by tight credit markets and an accompanying global economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 12-01-09 1155GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090112e51c000gm\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (brazil near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\